INSERT INTO `posts` VALUES ('1788518952113','The Thai Town Hosting the USS Abraham Lincoln After a Grueling Deployment','1788518952113','About 5,000 sailors flush with cash and looking for R&R will pour into the seaside resort','PATTAYA, Thailand—At the Hottuna Bar in this seaside town, owner Suchet Teewiang will open a second counter to serve up ice-cold beers. Other venues on Walking ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788518952113_img_1788578773801_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>PATTAYA, <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/thailand\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thailand</a>—At the Hottuna Bar in this seaside town, owner Suchet Teewiang will open a second counter to serve up ice-cold beers. Other venues on Walking Street, the city’s main drag, are staging DJ nights or bringing in extra hands to welcome the expected crowds.</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">Some 5,000 American sailors will pour into Pattaya starting Wednesday, when the USS Abraham Lincoln aircraft carrier and two other Navy ships make a five-day port call in eastern Thailand.</p>','Entrepreneurship','[\"News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788518952113_img_1788578773801_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',3,1790945067150,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Thai Town','The Thai Town Hosting the USS Abraham Lincoln After a Grueling Deployment','PATTAYA, Thailand—At the Hottuna Bar in this seaside town, owner Suchet Teewiang will open a second counter to serve up ice-cold beers. Other venues on Walking','[]'),('1788520751666','Washington’s Deadly New Headache: an al Qaeda-Houthi Terrorist Alliance','1788520751666','One man helped broker an arms trade between two militant groups that threatens another key oil-shipping route in the Middle East','On a balmy evening, Jibril “One-Armed” Yahya Ali and his new bride set out for a honeymoon drive along the beach outside al-Ghaydah, Yemen. Jibril, a Somali, an...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788520751666_img_1788578769295_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>On a balmy evening, Jibril “One-Armed” Yahya Ali and his new bride set out for a honeymoon drive along the beach outside al-Ghaydah, <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/iran-war-us-escalation-cycle-8d90061e?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Yemen</a>.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">Jibril, a Somali, and his Yemeni wife had met through a mutual acquaintance, an arms dealer who helped Jibril buy military-grade weapons from <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/yemen\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yemen</a>’s Houthi rebels. Jibril would then smuggle the arms to al-Shabaab, an Islamist insurgent group fighting to overthrow the government in Somalia.</p>','International News','[]','Home - Editors Picks','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788520751666_img_1788578769295_0.webp',NULL,'[\"asd\",\"qwe\"]','[]','5 min read',1,1790939771427,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Washington Deadly Headache Qaeda-Houthi','Washington’s Deadly New Headache: an al Qaeda-Houthi Terrorist Alliance','On a balmy evening, Jibril “One-Armed” Yahya Ali and his new bride set out for a honeymoon drive along the beach outside al-Ghaydah, Yemen. Jibril, a Somali, an','[]'),('1788521652439','U.S. Begins Deporting Immigrants to Liberia','1788521652439','The West African nation recently agreed with the Trump administration to accept up to 1,200 people in the next year','The U.S. has begun deporting immigrants to Liberia, officials in the West African country said, part of President Trump’s wider plan to send migrants to third-p...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The U.S. has begun deporting immigrants to Liberia, officials in the West African country said, part of President Trump’s wider plan to send migrants to third-party countries.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">A plane carrying an initial group of deportees landed Thursday at the Roberts International Airport, about 40 miles east of the capital in Monrovia, according to a spokesman for the Liberian government. The flight is part of a broader plan, announced by Liberian officials on Tuesday, for the country to take up to 1,200 deportees in the next year.&nbsp;</p><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788521652439_img_1788578764319_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;','Criminal Cases','[\"Golf\"]','Home - A+ Section 2','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788521652439_img_1788578764319_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1792061923644,'Oct 15, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Deporting Immigrants Liberia','U.S. Begins Deporting Immigrants to Liberia','The U.S. has begun deporting immigrants to Liberia, officials in the West African country said, part of President Trump’s wider plan to send migrants to third-p','[]'),('1788521879737','Kenya Helicopter Crash Leaves 7 Dead, Including 5 Americans','1788521879737','A Telemundo executive and an Ecuador intelligence chief are among the victims','Seven people, including five Americans, were killed in a helicopter crash in Kenya Wednesday, according to the State Department and local officials.The aircraft...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788521879737_img_1788578758900_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Seven people, including five Americans, were killed in a helicopter crash in Kenya Wednesday, according to the State Department and local officials.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The aircraft went down in Samburu County, Kenya, about eight hours north of Nairobi, a State Department spokesperson said. Seven people were aboard the helicopter, which crashed around 9:13 a.m. local time, according to Kenya’s Civil Aviation Authority. Samburu County Police Commander David Nkoroi said all seven died at the scene.</p>','World Politics','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788521879737_img_1788578758900_0.webp',NULL,'[\"asd\",\"zxc\"]','[]','5 min read',1,1791349882180,'Oct 7, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:01','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Kenya Helicopter Crash Including','Kenya Helicopter Crash Leaves 7 Dead, Including 5 Americans','Seven people, including five Americans, were killed in a helicopter crash in Kenya Wednesday, according to the State Department and local officials.The aircraft','[]'),('1788522069144','Pro-Business Leader Wins Re-Election in Zambia Vote Marred by Fraud Allegations','1788522069144','H.H., as supporters call him, plans to triple copper production by 2031','KAMPALA, Uganda— Zambian President Hakainde Hichilema, the pro-business leader of Africa’s No. 2 copper producer, won a second five-year term in a vote marred b...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788522069144_img_1788578754449_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>KAMPALA, Uganda— Zambian President Hakainde Hichilema, the pro-business leader of Africa’s No. 2 copper producer, won a second five-year term in a vote marred by opposition allegations of fraud and repression.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The 64-year-old economist and rancher, who entered the race widely expected to win, secured 61.4% of five million votes cast, well ahead of his closest rival, Brian Mundubile, who garnered 38%, the Electoral Commission of Zambia announced Tuesday. The wide margin of victory allowed Hichilema to avoid a runoff.</p>','CEOs & Executives','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788522069144_img_1788578754449_0.webp',NULL,'[\"srt\",\"ert\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790939641848,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Pro-Business Leader Zambia Vote','Pro-Business Leader Wins Re-Election in Zambia Vote Marred by Fraud Allegations','KAMPALA, Uganda— Zambian President Hakainde Hichilema, the pro-business leader of Africa’s No. 2 copper producer, won a second five-year term in a vote marred b','[]'),('1788523206790','The Paradox Behind the Relentless Spread of the Rare Ebola Strain','1788523206790','Bundibugyo variant replicates more slowly, meaning it can spread farther and kill more people before burning out','KAMPALA, Uganda—The scariest thing about the Ebola strain ripping through East Africa this year might be rather surprising: It isn’t quite as lethal as those in...','<figure style=\"float: none; margin: 24px auto; width: 450px; clear: both; max-width: 100%; display: block;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523206790_img_1788578748164_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>KAMPALA, Uganda—The scariest thing about <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/ebola-outbreak-explained-4ab4414f?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the Ebola strain</a> ripping through East Africa this year might be rather surprising: It isn’t quite as lethal as those in earlier outbreaks.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Previous variants were more dangerous on the face of it. People quickly fell ill and died during big outbreaks, like those in 2014 and 2018. But because Ebola strains like the Zaire variant were so lethal, they quickly ran out of new people to infect before they could move on to another area. They burned out.&nbsp;</p>','Currencies','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Trash','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788523206790.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788576438492,'Sep 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523305636','The Migrants Have Left Ceuta, but the Trauma Lingers','1788523305636','A city long-known as a melting pot of cultures suddenly feels vulnerable','EUTA, Spain—By Sunday morning, nearly all of the tens of thousands of migrants who flooded into this tiny Spanish city were gone. But the trauma of the sudden i...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523305636_img_1788578742707_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>EUTA, <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/spain\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Spain</a>—By Sunday morning, nearly all of the tens of thousands of migrants who flooded into this tiny Spanish city were gone. But the trauma of the sudden influx lingered.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Off a Mediterranean beach, countless shoes bobbed in the blue waters, abandoned by migrants <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/europe/spain-ceuta-migrants-c2d735e9?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">who had swum</a> to this slice of Spanish territory along the Strait of Gibraltar, just off the coast of <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/morocco\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Morocco</a>. Evaristo Casares Fernandez, a sanitation worker, noted that it would fall to him to clean up the floating mass of footwear.</p>','Business','[\"Politics\",\"World Politics\",\"Congress\",\"Elections\",\"Business\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523305636_img_1788578742707_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790426795412,'Sep 26, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"qwer@gmail.com\",\"asd@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523378203','Poor Countries Are Aging Fast but Can’t Keep Up With the Cost','1788523378203','Elderly populations are exploding in developing nations like Thailand, where savings and government resources are scant','NONG BUA HING, Thailand—Boonma Klahan starts her mornings by washing, changing and feeding her 85-year-old mother, who has dementia and spends her days on a mat...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523378203_img_1788578737076_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>NONG BUA HING, <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/thailand\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thailand</a>—Boonma Klahan starts her mornings by washing, changing and feeding her 85-year-old mother, who has dementia and spends her days on a mattress on the family home’s wooden floor.</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">She makes breakfast for her 87-year-old father and then rides her motorbike to her job as a health aide to 22 other elderly people in this poor farming village west of Bangkok. Three of Boonma’s charges are bedridden like her mother. Most of the others can no longer leave their homes.</p>','U.S. News','[\"Politics\",\"Legal Affairs\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523378203_img_1788578737076_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790618478908,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523449100','In Congo, Ebola Responders Fear WhatsApp Voice Notes Are Spreading Fake News','1788523449100','Recordings sent over Meta’s messaging app have potential to travel farther than text','KAMPALA, Uganda—An Ebola response team ran into an unexpected obstacle when they arrived to spray a roadside market with disinfectant a couple of weeks ago: the...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523449100_img_1788578732166_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>KAMPALA, Uganda—An Ebola response team ran into an unexpected obstacle when they arrived to spray a roadside market with disinfectant a couple of weeks ago: the admin for a local WhatsApp group.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">“You have come to spread Ebola in our village. You must leave now,” the young man said at his banana stall in Kasenyi in Irumu district, in the eastern reaches of the Democratic Republic of Congo, before pulling his Chinese-made Tecno smartphone to record a voice note, according to interviews with the volunteers from the local Boga Youth Council.</p>','Business','[\"Corporate News\",\"Small Business\",\"Entrepreneurship\",\"CEOs & Executives\",\"Markets & Finance\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523449100_img_1788578732166_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790157362824,'Sep 23, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523521024','Hundreds of Rohingya Feared Dead on World’s Riskiest Migrant Sea Route','1788523521024','Desperation in Bangladesh camps, years of war and persecution in Myanmar have pushed more refugees to attempt the perilous crossing','An estimated 500 migrants, most of them members of Myanmar’s persecuted Rohingya minority, are feared dead after two crowded ships sank within days of each othe...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523521024_img_1788578727553_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>An estimated 500 migrants, most of them members of <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/myanmar\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Myanmar</a>’s persecuted Rohingya minority, are feared dead after two crowded ships sank within days of each other off the coast of the war-torn country, the United Nations said Thursday.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The journey across the Andaman Sea and Bay of Bengal toward <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/malaysia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Malaysia</a> and Indonesia has in recent years seen more deaths than any maritime crossing other than the Mediterranean and the route between West Africa and Spain’s Canary Islands.</p>','Law','[\"Stocks\",\"Currencies\",\"Banking\",\"Economy\",\"Jobs & Employment\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523521024_img_1788578727553_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1789967045350,'Sep 21, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523619515','South African Vigilantes Chase Out Immigrants With Knives and Clubs','1788523619515','‘I don’t want to die here,’ says a woman waiting to return home','DURBAN, South Africa—For weeks, Ide Juma has slept on a thin mattress on the sidewalk outside the Department of Home Affairs refugee office in South Africa’s th...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 100%; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523619515_img_1788578723020_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>DURBAN, <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/south-africa\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">South Africa</a>—For weeks, Ide Juma has slept on a thin mattress on the sidewalk outside the Department of Home Affairs refugee office in <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/south-africa\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">South Africa</a>’s third-largest city, hoping against all experience that the authorities will protect him when the vigilantes come hunting for immigrants.</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">Juma, 35, a refugee from a war-torn corner of Mozambique, had been in South Africa—legally—for a decade. Then, a few months ago, members of an anti-immigrant group called March &amp; March cornered him outside the tented barbershop where he worked and beat him with sticks and clubs. Injured and too frightened to venture out to work, Juma fell behind on his rent and lost the room he was living in.</p>','Criminal Cases','[\"Interest Rates\",\"Tech\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Innovation\"]','Home - Top News','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523619515_img_1788578723020_0.webp',NULL,'[\"ert\"]','[]','5 min read',21,1789386416233,'Sep 14, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523684895','Ebola Is Devastating Congo. Uganda Found a Way to Stop It.','1788523684895','Aggressive measures to slow the spread of the infection have ruffled feathers, but they appear to be working','KAMPALA, Uganda—It was no surprise that the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo quickly jumped across the border into Uganda. Citizens of both co...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523684895_img_1788578717582_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>KAMPALA, Uganda—It was no surprise that the Ebola outbreak in the Democratic Republic of Congo quickly jumped across the border into Uganda. Citizens of both countries routinely cross over to do business and visit relatives.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The surprising part is that Uganda’s aggressive control methods appear to have stymied the spread of the deadly virus, in part by prohibiting people from hugging or even shaking hands.</p>','Editorials','[\"Personal Finance\",\"Opinion\",\"Research\",\"Environment\",\"Climate\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523684895_img_1788578717582_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789966707024,'Sep 21, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523757094','The Science Behind Venezuela’s Doublet Earthquake','1788523757094','The country sits at the point where the Caribbean Plate slides up against the South American Plate','The earthquakes that struck Venezuela on Wednesday night were a dangerous two-punch combination known as a doublet, collapsing buildings in the capital Caracas ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523757094_img_1788578709390_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>The <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/americas/venezuela-earthquakes-caracas-damage-a5835528?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">earthquakes that struck Venezuela</a> on Wednesday night were a dangerous two-punch combination known as a doublet, collapsing buildings in the capital Caracas and raising fears for the fate of the population in the worst-affected areas.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The first magnitude-7.2 shock struck near the town of San Felipe, west of Caracas. Data from the U.S. Geological Survey suggested it added stress to another nearby fault just over 3 miles away, triggering a larger magnitude-7.5 quake 39 seconds later. It was a relatively shallow, at a depth of 6 miles, and was felt as far away as northern Brazil.</p>','Opinions','[\"Space\",\"Science\",\"Cars\",\"Food & Dining\",\"Travel\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523757094_img_1788578709390_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1789965955688,'Sep 21, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523869076','In About-Face, Trump Administration Drops Opposition to Africa’s Antigay Laws','1788523869076','The U.S. has been silent on a law passed in Ghana last month in a sharp shift from the Biden years','JOHANNESBURG—The Trump administration is quietly reversing U.S. policy toward antigay laws being passed across Africa.When Uganda enacted one of the world’s str...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788523869076_img_1788578703656_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>JOHANNESBURG—The Trump administration is quietly reversing U.S. policy toward antigay laws being passed across Africa.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">When Uganda enacted one of the world’s <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/how-police-and-criminals-use-ugandas-antigay-law-to-find-blackmail-targets-93d4de43?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">strictest antigay laws</a> in 2023, the Biden administration imposed visa restrictions on its top officials and moved to cut off the country’s goods from U.S. markets. The Trump administration, in contrast, was silent last month when Ghana’s Parliament passed sweeping antigay legislation.</p>','Business','[\"Lifestyle\",\"Cricket\",\"Tennis\",\"Golf\",\"Soccer\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788523869076_img_1788578703656_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818935532,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788523944857','A Nation’s Soccer Hero: The Superfan Who Says He Can Stop Goals','1788523944857','Congolese man’s motionless presence is seen as so critical to the team’s success that the president intervened to get him to the U.S.','KAMPALA, Uganda—Michel Kuka Mboladinga is on a mission so critical that the president of the Democratic Republic of Congo personally intervened so he could carr...','<img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Fimages.wsj.net%2Fim-93421254%3Fwidth%3D1280%26height%3D853\" alt=\"Michel Kuka Mboladinga, pictured at a match in January, is known for his snappy suits and resemblance to his country’s founding prime minister.\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">KAMPALA, Uganda—Michel Kuka Mboladinga is on a mission so critical that the president of the Democratic Republic of Congo personally intervened so he could carry it out on his behalf.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">The task: stop the country’s World Cup opponents from scoring.&nbsp;</p>','World Politics','[\"Law\"]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Rejected','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788523944857_1791033748239_1791033748309.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1791033750954,'Oct 3, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'He',NULL,'KAMPALA, Uganda—Michel Kuka Mboladinga is on a mission so critical that the president of the Democratic Republic of Congo personally intervened so he could carr','[]'),('1788524096889','Congo’s Ebola Outbreak Reaches Territory Held by Islamic State','1788524096889','Militant violence creates no-go zone for health responders as virus spreads','NAIROBI—A rare strain of Ebola has reached a corner of the Democratic Republic of Congo controlled by Islamic State militants, a place too dangerous for health ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524096889_img_1788578697497_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>NAIROBI—A rare strain of Ebola has reached a corner of the Democratic Republic of Congo controlled by Islamic State militants, a place <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/as-ebola-spreads-in-congo-islamic-state-and-rebels-slow-rescue-efforts-bd224bd7?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">too dangerous for health workers</a> fighting to stop the deadly virus.</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">The Bundibugyo strain has killed one person in the militant-controlled territory of Mambasa, which is some 100 miles from the outbreak’s epicenter in a gold-mining town of Mongbwalu. Mambasa is the stronghold of the Allied Democratic Forces, an Islamic State affiliate conducting an insurgency against Congolese and Ugandan troops.</p>','Business','[\"Sports\",\"Mental Health\",\"Medical Research\",\"Health\",\"Crypto\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524096889_img_1788578697497_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818927437,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524162787','Ebola Outbreak Is Now Third Largest in History. Here’s What to Know.','1788524162787','Vaccine developers are moving quickly as a rare Ebola strain spreads in a volatile region of Democratic Republic of Congo','An outbreak of a rare strain of Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo is already the third largest in history, just weeks after it likely began.It is spread...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524162787_img_1788578692851_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>An outbreak of a rare strain of Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo is already the third largest in history, just weeks after it likely began.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">It is spreading rapidly in one of the most volatile and vulnerable regions of the world, worrying U.S. and international health officials. Cuts to international health aid over the past year and a half are adding to the burden, some public-health leaders say.</p>','Business','[\"Wealth Management\",\"Real Estate\",\"Investing\",\"Jewelry\",\"Designers\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524162787_img_1788578692851_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818919015,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524247121','Trump Wants Minerals, Health Data for Aid. African Nations Are Pushing Back.','1788524247121','Governments bridle at U.S. demands for private medical data and, in some cases, access to minerals','A handful of African nations are rejecting American health aid, outraged by the Trump administration’s demands for access to private health records and even min...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524247121_img_1788578688836_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>A handful of African nations are rejecting American health aid, outraged by the Trump administration’s demands for access to private health records and even minerals in exchange for lifesaving medicine.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">A year after President Trump reversed decades of American policy toward poor countries and closed the U.S. Agency for International Development, some African governments are bridling at the conditions he has set for resuming funding to combat AIDS, tuberculosis and malaria.</p>','Business','[\"Fashion\",\"Construction\",\"Agriculture\",\"Automotive\",\"Energy\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524247121_img_1788578688836_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818909454,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524329952','Court Blocks Trump Administration Plan to Treat American Ebola Patients in Kenya','1788524329952','Kenyan judge halts construction and operations of a tented U.S. field hospital','NAIROBI—A Kenyan high court put a temporary hold on the Trump administration’s plan to set up an Ebola quarantine-and-treatment facility for Americans in the Ea...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524329952_img_1788578684814_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>NAIROBI—A Kenyan high court put a temporary hold on the Trump administration’s plan to set up an Ebola quarantine-and-treatment facility for Americans in the East African country.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Hours after the U.S. said it had sealed a deal with Kenya to erect a tented field hospital on a Kenyan air base, the court on Friday halted construction and barred medical operations while a lawsuit objecting to the plan is pending.</p>','Business','[\"Industries\",\"Culture\",\"Books\",\"Architecture\",\"Upcoming Brands\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524329952_img_1788578684814_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818901432,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524403852','U.S. Says Deal Reached With Kenya on Ebola Quarantine Facility for Americans','1788524403852','Agreement comes amid local outrage in Kenya','The Trump administration said Thursday it had reached a deal with Kenya to establish a quarantine facility for Americans exposed to Ebola in the Democratic Repu...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524403852_img_1788578679584_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>The Trump administration said Thursday it had reached a deal with Kenya to establish a quarantine facility for Americans exposed to Ebola in the Democratic Republic of Congo, an arrangement that has drawn fierce opposition from Kenyan medical groups.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">In a conference call with reporters, senior administration officials said more than 30 U.S. public-health officers were en route to staff the 50-bed unit, which will be located at the Laikipia Air Base outside the city of Nanyuki and operational beginning Friday. The deployed officers include physicians, nurses, therapists and technologists, one of the officials said, including those who have experience dealing with prior Ebola outbreaks.</p>','Business','[\"Arts\",\"Celebrity\",\"Music\",\"Television\",\"Movies\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524403852_img_1788578679584_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818891929,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524472346','U.S. Races to Set Up Quarantine Facility in Kenya for Americans Exposed to Ebola','1788524472346','Move is a departure from procedure used during previous outbreaks of the virus','WASHINGTON—The Trump administration is expected to deploy U.S. public-health officers to Kenya to staff a potential quarantine facility there amid the Ebola out...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524472346_img_1788578674395_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—The Trump administration is expected to deploy U.S. public-health officers to Kenya to staff a potential quarantine facility there amid the <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/ebola-outbreak-explained-4ab4414f?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">Ebola outbreak</a> in the Democratic Republic of Congo, according to people familiar with the matter.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The people said the facility, which Tuesday was pending signoff from the Kenyan government, is primarily intended for Americans who are exposed to or at high risk of testing positive for the virus in the region, as well as Americans who test positive.</p>','Business','[\"Entertainment\",\"Innovation\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Tech\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524472346_img_1788578674395_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789818882778,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524545150','China Eliminates Tariffs on Africa to Outmaneuver Trump','1788524545150','Beijing’s ‘politically astute’ move contrasts with U.S. tariff barrage','JOHANNESBURG—African countries are finding it harder to export to the U.S. since President Trump returned to the White House with a long list of tariffs. But Ch...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524545150_img_1788578669958_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>JOHANNESBURG—African countries are finding it harder to export to the U.S. since President Trump returned to the White House with a long list of <a data-type=\"subject\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/subject/tariffs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tariffs</a>. But China sees their struggle as an opportunity.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Since May 1, Beijing has removed tariffs on all goods from 53 of 54 African nations in an effort to win business and influence across the continent. Everything from wine to sesame seeds and wool has been entering China tariff-free from everywhere except tiny Eswatini, which maintains diplomatic ties with Taiwan. Analysts say the move could push Africa’s population of more than a billion people and vast mineral resources further into China’s orbit.</p>','Business','[\"Interest Rates\",\"Jobs & Employment\",\"Economy\",\"Banking\",\"Currencies\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524545150_img_1788578669958_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1789818869696,'Sep 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524658873','Deep Distrust, Superstition Impede Efforts to Contain Ebola','1788524658873','Grieving families are fighting medical personnel for access to bodies as misinformation worsens the outbreak','NAIROBI—When Red Cross volunteers cocooned in hazmat suits and face shields arrived at a small hospital in the Democratic Republic of Congo this weekend to disp...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524658873_img_1788578664746_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>NAIROBI—When Red Cross volunteers cocooned in hazmat suits and face shields arrived at a small hospital in the Democratic Republic of Congo this weekend to dispose of the remains of a popular local preacher, they found themselves in a fast-escalating confrontation with relatives who insisted on touching the highly infectious corpse.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The volunteers waved the man’s family members away from <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/doctors-hospitals-struggle-to-keep-up-with-ebolas-spread-8a489864?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the Ebola isolation tent</a> at Mongbwalu General Hospital, where his body lay on a plastic sheet on the floor.</p>','Lifestyle','[\"Entertainment\",\"Innovation\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Cybersecurity\",\"Tech\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524658873_img_1788578664746_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789650687792,'Sep 17, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524744065','Doctors, Hospitals Struggle to Keep Up With Ebola’s Spread','1788524744065','‘Hospitals are fighting with no tools at all,’ says director-general of Africa’s CDC as fast-spreading Congo outbreak overwhelms resources','NAIROBI, Kenya—The fast-spreading Ebola virus is overwhelming creaking hospitals and clinics in the Democratic Republic of Congo, dimming hopes for quick contai...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524744065_img_1788578659963_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>NAIROBI, Kenya—The fast-spreading Ebola virus is overwhelming creaking hospitals and clinics in the Democratic Republic of Congo, dimming hopes for quick containment of what is already <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/world/africa/ebola-outbreak-explained-4ab4414f?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the third-largest outbreak</a> of the killer disease in history.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u ex0k10u0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">With at least 750 suspected cases and an official death count of 177 as of this weekend—the actual toll is likely higher—patients are being treated in ordinary wards because of a lack of dedicated Ebola treatment centers in the hardest-hit areas, according to the Africa Centers for Disease Control and Prevention.</p>','News','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524744065_img_1788578659963_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790619589415,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524836866','Vance’s 2028 Audition With Voters Has Begun','1788524836866','Plus, Sen. Fetterman is showing little interest in his job, and some Republicans worry about having Trump at the center of their midterms campaign','Good morning. The past couple of weeks have shown the gauntlet Vice President JD Vance will have to navigate if he seeks to sew up the GOP nomination for presid...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524836866_img_1788578655493_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-11kxzt3-Strong e1ofiv6m1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Good morning.</span> The past couple of weeks have shown the gauntlet Vice President JD Vance will have to navigate if he seeks to sew up the GOP nomination for president in 2028.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">He will need to stay close to President Trump while also owning the fact that he is not President Trump.</p>','International News','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524836866_img_1788578655493_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790620845843,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788524917705','Behind Closed Doors, John Fetterman Shows Little Interest in the Work of a Senator','1788524917705','Poised to be a possible swing vote in a divided Congress, he churns through staff as he dodges constituents, alienates fellow Democrats and courts Israel lobby','One morning in June, three paralyzed military veterans in wheelchairs from rural Pennsylvania arrived at the office of Sen. John Fetterman for a long-awaited me...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788524917705_img_1788578651460_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>One morning in June, three paralyzed military veterans in wheelchairs from rural <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/pennsylvania\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pennsylvania</a> arrived at the office of Sen. <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/john-fetterman\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">John Fetterman</a> for a long-awaited meeting to discuss legislation that would improve their care.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">Fetterman’s staff greeted them with bad news: The Pennsylvania Democrat had to cancel. He’d told his staff he may have eaten something bad and wasn’t feeling well, according to people familiar with the matter.</p>','U.S. News','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788524917705_img_1788578651460_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790621322696,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525050065','Missouri Supreme Court Rules State Can’t Use Redrawn Map in Midterms','1788525050065','Trump blasts the ruling, which is a blow to Republicans who were hoping to gain one House seat with new map','The Missouri Supreme Court ruled Thursday that the state can’t use redrawn congressional districts that could have benefited Republicans in November’s midterm e...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525050065_img_1788578646313_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>The Missouri Supreme Court ruled Thursday that the state can’t use redrawn congressional districts that could have <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/trumps-team-expands-redistricting-push-after-scoring-wins-in-court-0f51156c?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">benefited Republicans</a> in November’s midterm elections, and voters must decide if they should be used in future elections.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The unanimous decision was a blow to Republicans who were <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/republicans-are-worried-the-redistricting-fight-is-backfiring-d83f89a6?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">hoping to gain</a> one U.S. House seat with the redrawn map in the midterms. Around the country, both parties have been changing congressional maps hoping to gain an advantage in the House.</p>','News','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Rejected','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525050065_img_1788578646313_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790621474430,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525133588','Trump Names Adam Telle Acting Army Secretary After Driscoll Resignation','1788525133588','Telle is the current assistant secretary of the Army for civil works','President Trump named Adam Telle as acting Army secretary, succeeding Dan Driscoll, who resigned earlier this week after months of tension with Defense Secretar...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525133588_img_1788578641518_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>President Trump named Adam Telle as acting Army secretary, succeeding Dan Driscoll, who resigned earlier this week after months of tension with Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Trump said Telle, assistant secretary of the Army for civil works, would start in his new job immediately. “He is a Great Patriot, who is respected by all,” Trump said Thursday evening on Truth Social.</p>','International News','[\"News\",\"International News\",\"Criminal Cases\",\"Politics\",\"Congress\"]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Rejected','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525133588_img_1788578641518_0.webp',NULL,'[\"sdf\",\"dfg\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790641377692,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525213151','Trump Administration Again Asks Supreme Court to Allow New Mail Voting Rules','1788525213151','Latest appeal seeks to clear the way for the Postal Service to enforce the rules ahead of November’s midterm elections','WASHINGTON—The Trump administration’s bid to deploy the U.S. Postal Service to regulate mail-in ballots is back at the Supreme Court for the second time in as m...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525213151_img_1788578637104_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—The Trump administration’s bid to deploy the U.S. Postal Service to regulate mail-in ballots is back at the Supreme Court for the second time in as many weeks.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">In an <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.supremecourt.gov/DocketPDF/26/26A297/422948/20260903154027877_USPS%20Final%20Rule%20Stay%20and%20Appx.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">emergency appeal</a> on Thursday, the administration asked the high court to allow it to immediately implement proposed rules that would require states to hand over voter data and would give the Postal Service power to reject mail ballots that don’t comply with new conditions.</p>','U.S. News','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525213151_img_1788578637104_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790642293669,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525292691','Work on Trump’s 250-Foot Arch in Washington to Start in Next Two Weeks','1788525292691','Plan to build structure between the Lincoln Memorial and Arlington National Cemetery faces legal challenges','Excavation work on President Trump’s 250-foot-tall arch in Washington, is expected to start over the next two weeks, the administration said Thursday. The proje...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525292691_img_1788578631940_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Excavation work on President Trump’s 250-foot-tall arch in Washington, is expected to start over the next two weeks, the administration said Thursday.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The project, one of Trump’s many so-called beautification projects in the nation’s capital, is facing litigation. Opponents have argued Trump needs congressional approval to build it. The triumphal arch would block or disrupt the sightline of other monuments, critics have said.&nbsp;</p>','Law','[\"News\",\"International News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525292691_img_1788578631940_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',2,1790643091392,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"ishmithabimsarani@gmil.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525411237','Stocks Rally After Fed Official’s Comments on Holding Rates Steady','1788525411237','Plus, vibes from Trump and Vance, and the IRS looks to influence higher ed policies','This is an edition of the What’s News newsletter, which helps you catch up on the headlines and understand the news, free in your inbox daily. If you’re not sub...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525411237_img_1788578626754_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><em data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-i6hrxa-Italic e1ofiv6m0\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>This is an edition of the What’s News newsletter, which helps you catch up on the headlines and understand the news, free in your inbox daily. </em><em data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-i6hrxa-Italic e1ofiv6m0\">If you’re not subscribed, <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/newsletters/whats-news?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">sign up here</a>.</em></p><h4 data-type=\"hed\" class=\"css-1cpfs5z-Smallhed e1oou4m30\" style=\"--headline-font-color: #222222; --headline-link-hover-color: #0274b6; margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 500; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\">1. Stocks climbed and global bond yields retreated.</h4><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The market moves followed comments by Fed governor Christopher Waller, who said he would <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/finance/stocks/stocks-bonds-rally-after-dovish-fed-comments-b95763ae?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">support holding interest rates steady</a> if August inflation data supports it. The odds of a Fed rate increase this month are now a coin flip, according to CME FedWatch, down from a 70% likelihood yesterday. The Dow Jones Industrial Average rose 1.2%, the S&amp;P 500 added 1.1%, and the Nasdaq composite climbed 1.4%.</p>','Crypto','[\"U.S. News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525411237_img_1788578626754_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790642469287,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"oibyyapa@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525487156','Shock Defections Challenge Top Democrat Hakeem Jeffries','1788525487156','Two centrists side with Republicans on critical House vote, blindsiding the potential future speaker','WASHINGTON—The surprise defections of two Democrats on a Republican procedural vote has sparked soul-searching in the party and raised new questions about wheth...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525487156_img_1788578622371_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—The surprise defections of two Democrats on a Republican procedural vote has sparked soul-searching in the party and raised new questions about whether Minority Leader <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/hakeem-jeffries\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hakeem Jeffries</a>—the possible next House speaker—has the muscle to keep members in line.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">House Democrats were stunned when Reps. Jared Golden (D., Maine) and Marie Gluesenkamp Perez (D., Wash.), two centrist members, voted this week to narrowly advance a rules package by a 210-208 tally. That allowed Republicans to then move forward on a series of votes, including a resolution condemning socialism that was designed to embarrass Democrats. Members of the minority party rarely help the majority party pass such rules.</p>','Criminal Cases','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525487156_img_1788578622371_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790645269570,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"ishmithabimsarani@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525587803','Vance Defends Friendship With Trump Critic Tucker Carlson','1788525587803','Some Republicans have called on vice president to distance himself from former Fox News host','WASHINGTON—Vice President JD Vance defended his friendship with former Fox News host Tucker Carlson, rejecting pressure from some Republicans to distance himsel...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525587803_img_1788578618870_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—Vice President <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/jd-vance\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">JD Vance</a> defended his friendship with former Fox News host <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/tucker-carlson\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tucker Carlson</a>, rejecting pressure from some Republicans to distance himself from the conservative iconoclast.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">“Tucker is a friend, despite the fact that we disagree on a number of things,” Vance told reporters Thursday at the White House. “And I’m not going to play the game where I throw friends under the bus because I have political disagreements with them.”</p>','News','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525587803_img_1788578618870_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1790645462433,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788525817064','Leon Black Sues House Committee Over Epstein Probe','1788525817064','Billionaire won’t appear before House panel, claims it cannot compel him to turn over nondisclosure agreements with women','Leon Black is suing the House Oversight Committee probing his ties with Jeffrey Epstein and refusing to turn over some nondisclosure agreements, arguing the pan...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788525817064_img_1788578615109_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Leon Black is suing the House Oversight Committee probing his ties with Jeffrey Epstein and refusing to turn over some nondisclosure agreements, arguing the panel and its chair have overstepped their authority.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Black, the co-founder of <span style=\"display: unset;\"><a data-type=\"company\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/APO\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Apollo Global Management</a></span>, was scheduled to appear Thursday before the Oversight Committee for a second round of questioning. He won’t appear. Instead, he filed a lawsuit in federal court against the committee and its Republican chair, Rep. James Comer (R., Ky.).</p>','CEOs & Executives','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788525817064_img_1788578615109_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1791294092077,'Oct 6, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[\"akramyoonos006@gmail.com\"]',1,'Leon Black House Committee','Leon Black Sues House Committee Over Epstein Probe','Leon Black is suing the House Oversight Committee probing his ties with Jeffrey Epstein and refusing to turn over some nondisclosure agreements, arguing the pan','[]'),('1788526095992','Tillis Wants Hegseth Fired. Is the Pentagon Chief in Trouble?','1788526095992','Plus, the U.S.’s nuclear deal with Saudi Arabia includes a road map for enriching uranium, and the odd political alliance opposing data centers','Good morning. The aftershocks of Army Secretary Dan Driscoll’s resignation this week continue to rumble.On Wednesday, Sen. Thom Tillis (R., N.C.) called for Pre...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526095992_img_1788578610985_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-11kxzt3-Strong e1ofiv6m1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Good morning.</span> The aftershocks of Army Secretary Dan Driscoll’s <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/national-security/army-secretary-resigns-after-months-of-friction-with-hegseth-9c124207?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">resignation this week</a> continue to rumble.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">On Wednesday, Sen. <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/thom-tillis\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Thom Tillis</a> (R., N.C.) called for President Trump to replace Defense Secretary <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/pete-hegseth\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pete Hegseth</a>. The retiring senator’s <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://x.com/SenThomTillis/status/2095175195648512020\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">critique of the Pentagon chief</a> was harsh.</p>','Business','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Draft','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788526095992.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788576426511,'Sep 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788526219019','Hegseth Extends Mideast Deployments Into 2027, Escalating Strain on Troops','1788526219019','Trump has told aides privately that he believes his strategy will eventually work, as 50,000 troops remain on hand to give him options','When the U.S. launched its campaign against Iran six months ago, Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth promised a quick, decisive blow that would avoid a long entangle...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526219019_img_1788578606582_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>When the U.S. launched its campaign against <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/iran\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Iran</a> six months ago, Defense Secretary <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/pete-hegseth\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pete Hegseth</a> promised a quick, decisive blow that would avoid a long entanglement. Now, he is quietly extending troop deployments in a sign that the conflict could drag well into next year, according to people familiar with the matter.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">It is part of an open-ended military strategy designed to give President Trump options in the war, the people said. But the deployment of 19 warships, air-defense units, fighter squadrons and paratroopers across the region is straining servicemembers and their families and creating a maintenance backlog that could take years to unwind, the people said.</p>','Business','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Draft','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788526219019.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788576426028,'Sep 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788526414460','Ted Cruz Is Testing the Waters for a 2028 Run—and Taking Swipes at JD Vance','1788526414460','The Texas senator is making trips to Iowa, promoting his book and hitting the podcast circuit as he considers joining the race to succeed Trum','CLIVE, Iowa—Ted Cruz isn’t hiding his presidential ambitions—and he is taking some digs at the presumptive front-runner along the way.The 2028 contest hasn’t st...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526414460_img_1788578602485_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>CLIVE, <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/iowa\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Iowa</a>—<a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/ted-cruz\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Ted Cruz</a> isn’t hiding his presidential ambitions—and he is taking some digs at the presumptive front-runner along the way.</p><p class=\"emoyrq42 e1bc1vag0 css-1uzoyz5-StyledNewsKitParagraph\" data-type=\"paragraph\" data-testid=\"paragraph\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; margin: 0px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-stretch: normal; margin-block-end: 16px; word-break: break-word; line-height: calc(1.55556);\">The 2028 contest hasn’t started yet, and there is still a <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/republicans-are-worried-about-the-midterms-trump-is-focused-on-his-legacy-597e5512?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">midterm election</a> in November. Vice President JD Vance, who is leading in early polls of potential Republican nominees, is campaigning for candidates in tough races and <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/elections/an-88-600-photo-with-trump-gop-hopes-to-raise-millions-during-convention-ea336f52?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">fundraising for the party</a>.</p>','Business','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Draft','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788526414460.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788576425503,'Sep 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788526693387','Sen. Ed Markey Trounces Younger Challenger in Massachusetts','1788526693387','The 80-year-old prevails in the Democratic primary over Rep. Seth Moulton','WASHINGTON—Massachusetts Sen. Ed Markey, who has spent nearly half a century in Congress, easily beat back a Democratic primary challenge Tuesday from Rep. Seth...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526693387_img_1788578598044_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—<a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/massachussetts\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Massachusetts</a> Sen. Ed Markey, who has spent nearly half a century in Congress, easily beat back a Democratic primary challenge Tuesday from Rep. Seth Moulton in a generational fight that focused on Markey’s age and the future of the party.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Markey, an 80-year-old liberal who has focused on climate change, defeated Moulton, a 47-year-old congressman who has frequently tangled with establishment figures within the party.</p>','Business','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Draft','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788526693387.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788576425144,'Sep 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788526872072','Do Democrats Have a Hasan Piker Problem?','1788526872072','Plus, the Postal Service faces mail-ballot allegations, and the U.S. renews strikes on Iran',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526872072_img_1788578594225_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-11kxzt3-Strong e1ofiv6m1\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Good morning.</span> Hasan Piker, an online streamer and unapologetic provocateur, has emerged as a <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/hasan-piker-twitch-democrats-a5aa0cd6?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">polarizing figure</a> in this 2026 election cycle. He is forcing Democrats to wrestle with a very uncomfortable question: How <em data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-i6hrxa-Italic e1ofiv6m0\">fringe</em> are they willing to become?</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Piker has said controversial things that have been well-documented about Sept. 11 and American Jews, among other things. Many Democrats try to wave him away. But he’s not a nobody. He has campaigned with Abdul El-Sayed, a bit of a provocateur himself who also happens to be the Democrats’ candidate for Senate in Michigan. Piker was at El-Sayed’s primary election night party and even <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://x.com/cspan/status/2094444361211642088\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">spoke to the cameras</a> after El-Sayed won.</p>','News','[\"U.S. News\",\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"International News\",\"Criminal Cases\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon',NULL,'Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788526872072_img_1788578594225_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790513177776,'Sep 27, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"qwe@gmail.com\",\"asd@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788526995928','What to Know About Mail-Ballot Allegations Against the Postal Service','1788526995928','An anonymous complaint and fast-moving litigation challenge Trump administration’s claims that it can implement rules without disruption','A Democratic senator on Tuesday released whistleblower allegations that the U.S. Postal Service has botched its implementation of mail-in ballot restrictions, a...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788526995928_img_1788578590081_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>A Democratic senator on Tuesday released whistleblower allegations that the U.S. Postal Service has botched its implementation of mail-in ballot restrictions, a move that comes as the Trump administration plays defense in court over the legality of the new regulations.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The litigation could be back in front of the Supreme Court in a matter of days or weeks, casting uncertainty over a method of voting used by one in three Americans that nevertheless has come in for sharp criticism by President Trump.</p>','Interviews','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788526995928_img_1788578590081_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1791213679958,'Oct 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Allegations Postal Service','What to Know About Mail-Ballot Allegations Against the Postal Service','A Democratic senator on Tuesday released whistleblower allegations that the U.S. Postal Service has botched its implementation of mail-in ballot restrictions, a','[]'),('1788527079269','House Passes Measure Funding Government Past the Midterms','1788527079269','Republicans and Democrats are eager to avoid another shutdown drama as they focus on re-election','WASHINGTON—The House overwhelmingly passed a bipartisan resolution to fund the government past a Sept. 30 deadline, with both Democrats and Republicans eager to...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788527079269_img_1788578585687_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—The House overwhelmingly passed a bipartisan resolution to fund the government past a Sept. 30 deadline, with both Democrats and Republicans eager to avoid a shutdown and leave Washington as soon as possible to campaign ahead of the midterms.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The resolution, which passed 370-48, extends current funding levels through Dec. 11. The Senate passed the stopgap spending bill last month, and it now goes to President Trump’s desk.</p>','Opinions','[]',NULL,'Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Pending review','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788527079269_img_1788578585687_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790946780440,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'House Government Past',NULL,'WASHINGTON—The House overwhelmingly passed a bipartisan resolution to fund the government past a Sept. 30 deadline, with both Democrats and Republicans eager to','[]'),('1788527736668','An $88,600 Photo With Trump: GOP Hopes to Raise Millions During Convention','1788527736668','Republican National Committee plans pair of high-dollar fundraisers during this month’s midterm convention in Dallas','WASHINGTON—Republicans are planning to raise millions of dollars during the coming GOP midterm convention in Dallas, including asking donors to pay more than $8...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788527736668_img_1788578580781_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>WASHINGTON—Republicans are planning to raise millions of dollars during the coming GOP midterm convention in <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/dallas\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dallas</a>, including asking donors to pay more than $88,000 for a photo with President Trump.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The Republican National Committee sent out invitations this week to a pair of fundraising events during the convention. A roundtable with Trump on Sept. 9 will cost $250,000 a person to attend, according to the invitation, which was reviewed by The Wall Street Journal. Donors can also take a photo with the president for $88,600.</p>','Congress','[\"Law\",\"News\",\"Politics\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788527736668_img_1788578580781_0.webp',NULL,'[\"dfg\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1792489538420,'Oct 20, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 09:45:38','[]',1,'GOP Raise Millions During','An $88,600 Photo With Trump: GOP Hopes to Raise Millions During Convention','WASHINGTON—Republicans are planning to raise millions of dollars during the coming GOP midterm convention in Dallas, including asking donors to pay more than $8','[]'),('1788579705326','plmokn ijb uhvy uygy igyf','1788579705326','rftyuio','e6 yg 7gs','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788579705326_img_1788579708003_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;e6 yg&nbsp; 7gs','Business','[]',NULL,'Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Trash','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788579705326.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788579710258,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788584194866','American Workers Have Slammed the Brakes on Switching Jobs','1788584194866','The country is adding around 80,000 jobs a month, up from last year, but workers are still wary','American workers are staying put. Workers across all sectors are switching jobs about as infrequently as they were in the years when the job market was still cl...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788584194866_img_1788584779277_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>American workers are staying put.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Workers across all sectors are switching jobs about as infrequently as they were in the years when the job market was still clawing its way back from the 2008-09 financial crisis. The “separation” rate, which includes both people who are laid off and those who leave their jobs voluntarily, has been stuck around its lowest levels since the years after the financial crisis. The flip side of that, the hiring rate, is similarly low.</p>','News','[\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"World Politics\",\"Elections\",\"International News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788584194866_img_1788584779277_0.webp',NULL,'[\"financial crisi\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1792414353633,'Oct 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'American Workers Switching Jobs','American Workers Have Slammed the Brakes on Switching Jobs','American workers are staying put. Workers across all sectors are switching jobs about as infrequently as they were in the years when the job market was still cl','[]'),('1788584668001','Time Is No Longer on Iran’s Side in the Battle of the Blockades','1788584668001','The U.S. is helping Gulf states move significant amounts of oil out of the region while thwarting Tehran’s shipments','DUBAI—By squeezing the Strait of Hormuz, both the U.S. and Iran expected to outlast their foe, believing time would work in their favor.Now, it looks like the t...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788584668001_img_1788584777341_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>DUBAI—By squeezing the Strait of Hormuz, both the U.S. and <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/iran\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Iran</a> expected to outlast their foe, believing time would work in their favor.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Now, it looks like the trend is moving against Tehran.</p>','U.S. News','[\"International News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788584668001_img_1788584777341_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',5,1791176638690,'Oct 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Time Iran','Time Is No Longer on Iran’s Side in the Battle of the Blockades','DUBAI—By squeezing the Strait of Hormuz, both the U.S. and Iran expected to outlast their foe, believing time would work in their favor.Now, it looks like the t','[]'),('1788584769563','‘Frederick Douglass’s American Founding’ and ‘Until the Last Yoke Is Broken’: A Foundational Question','1788584769563','Frederick Douglass’s early speeches condemned the U.S. Constitution for embedding slavery in its clauses. Decades later, he saw the document very differently.','Is the Constitution—the original one of 1787, before the later rights-extending amendments—pro-slavery or antislavery? The question was an urgent one to America...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788584769563_img_1788584773029_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Is the Constitution—the original one of 1787, before the later rights-extending amendments—pro-slavery or antislavery? The question was an urgent one to Americans amid the rising tensions leading up to the Civil War.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">As a young abolitionist, Frederick Douglass (1818-95) denounced the Constitution as “nothing more than a compromise with man-stealers, and a cunningly devised complication of falsehoods, calculated to deceive foreign nations into a belief that this is a free country.” By the early 1850s, however, he had reversed himself. Properly interpreted, he declared, the Constitution was “a glorious liberty document.” That startling conversion is the subject of Dennis C. Rasmussen’s “Frederick Douglass’s American Founding,” an engaging, lucid intellectual history. Bradley N. Rebeiro’s “Until the Last Yoke Is Broken” asks the next question: What constitutional theory allowed Douglass to reach so unlikely a conclusion?</p>','Congress','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Trash','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788584769563_img_1788584773029_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788585164044,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788584927839','‘By Any Means’ Review: Mark Wahlberg’s Gangster for a Good Cause','1788584927839','The actor stars alongside Yahya Abdul-Mateen II as a mob hitman enlisted by the FBI to help investigate a racist murder in 1960s Mississippi in this bare-knuckle historical drama.','“By Any Means” suggests it takes a dirty man to clean up a historically and culturally entrenched mess. We’re in 1966 Mississippi, where a straitlaced black FBI...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788584927839_img_1788584941520_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>“By Any Means” suggests it takes a dirty man to clean up a historically and culturally entrenched mess. We’re in 1966 <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/mississippi\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Mississippi</a>, where a straitlaced black FBI agent (Yahya Abdul-Mateen II) and a career criminal (Mark Wahlberg) become unlikely partners in an effort to solve a racist murder. Welcome to a race-swapped “48 Hrs.” with a heart of righteous fury.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Civil-rights dramas tend to be preachy and self-congratulatory, painting halos on the white saviors and the black victims, but the rousing “By Any Means” takes a literally punchy approach. It filters the trauma of race-based suffering through a genre piece about busting heads. Setting out to rebut the sanctimony of, say, “To Kill a Mockingbird,” with its holy glow, the feature directed by Elegance Bratton (“The Inspection”) has more of a “Dirty Harry” vibe. In a system corrupted by racism, justice is sometimes unattainable. If they mess with you, notes Mr. Wahlberg’s character, you’re allowed to mess with them, except he uses a different verb than “mess.”</p>','U.S. News','[\"News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788584927839_img_1788584941520_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1792413168157,'Oct 19, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Means','‘By Any Means’ Review: Mark Wahlberg’s Gangster for a Good Cause','“By Any Means” suggests it takes a dirty man to clean up a historically and culturally entrenched mess. We’re in 1966 Mississippi, where a straitlaced black FBI','[]'),('1788586575812','Fetterman Could Be a Swing Vote. He’s Showing Little Interest in the Job.','1788586575812','Plus, Elon Musk’s Boring Co. pushes investors for business help, and America has arrived at the Age of Millionaires','1. FROM MY DESKJohn Fetterman’s blue-collar wardrobe and plain-spoken progressivism once made him a star. Now, the Pennsylvania senator is showing little intere...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788586575812_img_1788586589698_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><h4 data-type=\"hed\" class=\"css-1cpfs5z-Smallhed e1oou4m30\" style=\"--headline-font-color: #222222; --headline-link-hover-color: #0274b6; margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 500; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>1. FROM MY DESK</h4><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-11kxzt3-Strong e1ofiv6m1\">John Fetterman’s blue-collar wardrobe and plain-spoken progressivism once made him a star.</span> Now, the Pennsylvania senator <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/john-fetterman-little-interest-senator-be74e7a3?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\">is showing little interest</a> in doing his job beyond cultivating relationships with conservative media figures and advocating for Israel. Interviews with more than a dozen former aides and lawmakers, along with internal records, show an increasingly dysfunctional operation as Fetterman churns through staff and dodges constituents. With a pivotal election looming that could give him outsize influence in Congress, Will Hobson and Siobhan Hughes report on the senator’s shifting politics—and his growing distance from fellow Democrats.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><em data-type=\"emphasis\" class=\"css-i6hrxa-Italic e1ofiv6m0\">This is an edition of The 10-Point newsletter, a guided tour of the best coverage in The Wall Street Journal. If you’re not subscribed, <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/newsletters/the-10-point?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">sign up here</a>. If you’re reading this in your inbox, tap the headline above for online and audio versions of this newsletter.</em></p>','Business','[\"Legal Affairs\",\"Politics\"]','Home - Editors Picks','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788586575812_img_1788586589698_0.webp',NULL,'[\"wall\",\"street\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1791032223669,'Oct 3, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Fetterman He Showing Little','Fetterman Could Be a Swing Vote. He’s Showing Little Interest in the Job.','1. FROM MY DESKJohn Fetterman’s blue-collar wardrobe and plain-spoken progressivism once made him a star. Now, the Pennsylvania senator is showing little intere','[]'),('1788608069595','The NFL’s $230 Million Bust Is Now Its Bargain Reclamation Project','1788608069595','The Vikings are betting that former No. 1 draft pick Kyler Murray can be their starting quarterback. And there’s almost no downside: His previous team is footing most of the bill.','By the end of last season, the Arizona Cardinals decided that they’d seen enough of their franchise quarterback. They were so ready to get rid of him that they ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788608069595_img_1788608074308_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>By the end of last season, the Arizona Cardinals decided that they’d seen enough of their franchise quarterback. They were so ready to get rid of him that they were willing to eat tens of millions of dollars to cut him loose.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Now, the <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/minnesota\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Minnesota</a> Vikings are betting that when it comes to Kyler Murray, one team’s potential blunder could be another team’s bargain.</p>','Sports','[\"International News\",\"World Politics\",\"Business\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788608069595_img_1788608074308_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1791120974724,'Oct 4, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'NFL Million Bust Now','The NFL’s $230 Million Bust Is Now Its Bargain Reclamation Project','By the end of last season, the Arizona Cardinals decided that they’d seen enough of their franchise quarterback. They were so ready to get rid of him that they','[]'),('1788608416173','The Hush-Hush Demands and Phony Endorsements That Rocked the NBA','1788608416173','A representative for NBA superstar Kawhi Leonard wanted extra money beyond league rules. An investigation says that the Los Angeles Clippers went to extreme lengths to accommodate him.','The NBA had just shut down due to the global pandemic when a star player’s business manager approached the Los Angeles Clippers with an unusual demand.While are...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788608416173_img_1788608419445_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>The NBA had just shut down due to the global pandemic when a star player’s business manager approached the <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/los-angeles\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Los Angeles</a> Clippers with an unusual demand.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">While arenas sat empty and the sport sat idle, a representative for Clippers superstar Kawhi Leonard named Dennis Robertson wanted $10 million more dollars a year for his client. Never mind that the team, owned by former Microsoft CEO Steve Ballmer, was already paying Leonard the maximum allowed under the NBA’s salary-cap rules.&nbsp;</p>','Sports','[\"Personal Finance\",\"Editorials\",\"Opinion\",\"Research\",\"Environment\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788608416173_img_1788608419445_0.webp',NULL,'[]'