adius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">Garrett Clark and his buddies spent years building an ultra popular YouTube channel devoted to their love of golf. They called it, simply, “Good Good.”&nbsp;</span><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">With their jokey, back-slapping attitude, they pulled off viral stunts, filmed themselves on storied courses, and gained enough followers to shoot videos with the likes of NBA superstar Stephen Curry and two-time major champion Bryson DeChambeau. Good Good, which launched its own apparel brand, had received tens of millions in investment and even struck a deal to sponsor a PGA Tour event later this year.&nbsp;</p>','Lifestyle','[\"Entrepreneurship\",\"Corporate News\",\"Elections\",\"Congress\",\"Business\"]','Home - Top News','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788609863929_img_1788609867178_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',5,1788841109961,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788609931960','There’s a U.S.-Canada Border War—in Bass Fishing','1788609931960','The race for Bassmaster’s ‘Angler of the Year’ is down to a beloved Canadian pro versus a game-changing phenom from Illinois, battling it out on Lake Ontario','The race for Bassmaster’s ‘Angler of the Year’ is down to a beloved Canadian pro versus a game-changing phenom from Illinois, battling it out on Lake Ontario','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8p