p News','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788610149722_1792078267889_1792078268860.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',14,1792078267775,'Oct 15, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 15:47:05','[]',1,'Contrarian Who Built NFL','The Contrarian Who Built the NFL’s Best Team by Investing Like Warren Buffett','Les Snead had been working in professional football for three decades when he realized that he’d been doing it all wrong.The general manager of the Los Angeles','[]'),('1788610222471','European Officials Seek Subpoena for Joshua Kushner on Infantino’s FIFA Selloff Plan','1788610222471','UEFA filed in New York on Thursday in preparation for possible criminal action against the FIFA president in Switzerland','The fallout from FIFA’s ill-fated plan to privatize part of its commercial rights and sell them to investors landed in New York district court on Thursday as UE...','<img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Fimages.wsj.net%2Fim-99795944%3Fsize%3D1.5%26width%3D161%26height%3D90\" alt=\"Behind Closed Doors, John Fetterman Shows Little Interest in the Work of a Senator\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The fallout from FIFA’s ill-fated plan to privatize part of its commercial rights and sell them to investors landed in <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/new-york\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">New York</a> district court on Thursday as UEFA, European soccer’s governing body, requested subpoenas for Joshua Kushner and his fund Thrive Capital Management.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">UEFA said that it hoped to use the documents in a criminal proceeding against FIFA president Gianni Infantino in <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/switzerland\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Switzerland</a>. In a separate filing in Florida, attorneys for the organization also requested documents specifically from FIFA, which keeps an office in Miami.</p>','Lifestyle','[\"Arts\",\"Architecture\",\"Culture\",\"Energy\",\"Manufacturing\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788610222471_1791030416951_1791030417679.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1791030416897,'Oct 3, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"ishmithabimsarani@gmail.com\"]',1,'FIFA Plan','European Officials Seek Subpoena for Joshua Kushner on Infantino’s FIFA Selloff Plan','The fallout from FIFA’s ill-fated plan to privatize part of its commercial rights and sell them to investors landed in New York district court on Thursday as UE','[]'),('1788610281873','The Mad Genius Taking College Football to Warp Speed','1788610281873','Alex Golesh only discovered the game after emigrating to the U.S. from the Soviet Union. Now he’s the outsider reshaping Auburn football.','When Alex Golesh fled the Soviet Union with his family at the age of 7, he didn’t speak a word of English. So when he turned on a TV in Brooklyn and saw grown m...','<img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Fimages.wsj.net%2Fim-53480628%3Fwidth%3D700%26height%3D467\" alt=\"Alex Golesh is the new head football coach at Auburn.\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">When Alex Golesh fled the Soviet Union with his family at the age of 7, he didn’t speak a word of English. So when he turned on a TV in Brooklyn and saw grown men bashing into each other over an oblong ball, he had no idea what to make of it.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">All this Russian grade schooler knew was that he liked it.</p>','U.S. News','[\"Construction\",\"Designers\",\"Investing\",\"Wealth Management\",\"Health\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_1788610281873_1791032014812_1791032015556.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1791032014757,'Oct 3, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:02','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',0,'Mad Genius Taking College','The Mad Genius Taking College Football to Warp Speed','When Alex Golesh fled the Soviet Union with his family at the age of 7, he didn’t speak a word of English. So when he turned on a 