retary Lori Chavez-DeRemer allowed harassment of staffers, had an inappropriate relationship with a security aide and used government funds for personal travel.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Released months after Chavez-DeRemer <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/labor-secretary-resigns-after-tumultuous-tenure-21d256e0?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">resigned under a cloud of allegations</a>, the 40-page report by the department’s internal watchdog described a “toxic, intimidating and humiliating” workplace at the federal agency tasked with protecting U.S. workers. The department also didn’t appear to have a policy addressing personal or romantic relationships between supervisors and subordinates, it found.&nbsp;</p>','Opinions','[\"Lifestyle\",\"Tennis\",\"Soccer\",\"Mental Health\",\"Health\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611443381_img_1788611445986_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788841127553,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788611516931','Energy & Utilities Roundup: Market Talk','1788611516931','1559 ET – Crude futures settle higher in a choppy session ahead of the U.S. Labor Day long weekend','closing out a week of gains that saw the resumption of U.S. strikes on Iranian targets and Iranian attacks on shipping. Oil price gains have been tempered by li...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611516931_img_1788611519140_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">closing out a week of gains that saw the resumption of U.S. strikes on Iranian targets and Iranian attacks on shipping. Oil price gains have been tempered by limited flows getting through the Strait of Hormuz, although differences remain on how much oil is making it out. A bigger-than-expected 4.5 million barrel draw in U.S. crude stocks reported midweek by the EIA added upside pressure. WTI settles up 0.2% at $91.48 a barrel, up 9.7% on the week. Brent rises 0.8% to $96.28, or 9.3% higher than a week ago.(anthony.harrup@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Wealth Management\",\"Investing\",\"Designers\",\"Construction\",\"Manufacturing\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611516931_img_1788611519140_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612206286,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788611589238','Auto & Transport Roundup: Market Talk','1788611589238','903 ET – Volkswagen’s restructuring agreement is a major positive surprise','proves the company can implement its transformation program despite complex governance and labor constraints, Bank of America Securities analysts Horst Schneide...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611589238_img_1788611592820_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">proves the company can implement its transformation program despite complex governance and labor constraints, Bank of America Securities analysts Horst Schneider and Stephen Benhamou write. Ahead of the meeting, media reports had suggested an escalating confrontation with labor and state representatives, potentially culminating in legal action or an extraordinary general meeting, the bank says. “Against this backdrop, we believe few expected a unanimous agreement.” The plan envisages around 50,000 additional job reductions globally by 2030, taking the total number to 100,000, but the detailed measures still need to be agreed. It is therefore not yet clear when restructuring provisions will be booked, but the bank estimates gross charges of up to 10 billion euros, probably spread over several years. Shares rise 7.6%. (dominic.chopping@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Energy\",\"Culture\",\"Architecture\",\"Arts\",\"Music\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611589238_img_1788611592820_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612198200,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788611658413','Basic Materials Roundup: Market Talk','1788611658413','1437 ET – Gold futures fell as U.S. payrolls increased well above expectations in August, pushing up short-term Treasury yields and raising expectations of a possible September Fed hike.','President Trump, however, called for lower interest rates following the employment report. “A resilient labor market would give the Fed permission to move rates...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611658413_img_1788611661803_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;President Trump, however, called for lower interest rates following the employment report. “A resilient labor market would give the Fed permission to move rates higher at the September meeting if upcoming August inflation data does not show continued improvement, but that political pressure to maintain lower rates looms in the background,” Mike Castle of StoneX says in a note. Front month gold settles down 1.4% at $4,429.80 a troy ounce for a 1.1% loss on the week. Silver falls 1.4% to $66.047, also a 1.4% weekly loss. (anthony.harrup@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Movies\",\"Innovation\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Interest Rates\",\"Economy\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611658413_img_1788611661803_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612177867,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788611904929','Tech, Media & Telecom Roundup: Market Talk','1788611904929','1541 ET – Adobe’s appointment of Anil Chakravarthy as its next CEO may signal a shift in the company’s focus, especially as investors worry that Creative Cloud is exposed to AI displacement, Morgan Stanley analysts write in a note.','The move “could signal that Adobe’s center of gravity is shifting toward customer experience, enterprise workflows, and content supply chains, rather than relyi...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611904929_img_1788611908062_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">The move “could signal that Adobe’s center of gravity is shifting toward customer experience, enterprise workflows, and content supply chains, rather than relying on Creative Cloud as the primary growth engine,” the analysts write. “We see that as potentially the right strategic direction.” Still, they say, the appointment does not necessarily mean a “wholesale deprioritization of Creative,” but suggests that Adobe “could now be attempting to turn CX orchestration into a larger growth and monetization engine for enterprises.” Adobe shares trade down 6.4%. (elias.schisgall@wsj.com)</span>','Business','[\"Currencies\",\"Markets & Finance\",\"Entrepreneurship\",\"Corporate News\",\"Congress\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611904929_img_1788611908062_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612161587,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788611992391','Democrats Criticize Fetterman After WSJ Report on How He Spends His Time','1788611992391','Plus, the DOJ told its antitrust division to pause work with Canada, and diesel hits an all-time high','1. Democratic lawmakers and activists criticized John Fetterman after a WSJ report found he has been shirking his duties as a U.S. senator for Pennsylvania.“202...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788611992391_img_1788611995675_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><h4 data-type=\"hed\" class=\"css-1cpfs5z-Smallhed e1oou4m30\" style=\"--headline-font-color: #222222; --headline-link-hover-color: #0274b6; margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; font-weight: 500; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>1. Democratic lawmakers and activists criticized John Fetterman after a WSJ report found he has been shirking his duties as a U.S. senator for Pennsylvania.</h4><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">“<a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/democrats-assail-fetterman-after-wsj-report-9a60e499?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">2028 can’t come soon enough</a>,” said Pennsylvania state Rep. Malcolm Kenyatta, who is also a vice chair of the Democratic National Committee. The Journal’s reporting, based on text messages from the senator and interviews with former staffers and others, <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/john-fetterman-little-interest-senator-be74e7a3?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">showed he has little interest</a> in meeting with constituents, attending in-state events or sitting through Senate hearings. Short on time? <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/politics/policy/takeaways-from-wsjs-reporting-on-john-fetterman-2b43e666?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Read our key takeaways</a>.</p>','Business','[\"Politics\",\"Criminal Cases\",\"International News\",\"News\",\"U.S. News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788611992391_img_1788611995675_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612140902,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788612054956','Record Fuel Prices Pose Fresh Challenge for Trump Ahead of Midterms','1788612054956','Diesel hits an average $5.85 a gallon on Friday, an all-time high that surpasses the previous record from 2022','President Trump came into office pledging to lower energy prices for Americans. Instead, he is presiding over a historic run-up in fuel prices. Diesel prices hi...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788612054956_img_1788612057487_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>President Trump came into office pledging to <a data-type=\"link\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/economy/central-banking/donald-trump-energy-interest-rates-312cfc24?mod=article_inline\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">lower energy prices</a> for Americans. Instead, he is presiding over a historic run-up in fuel prices.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">Diesel prices hit an average $5.85 a gallon on Friday, according to OPIS, a Dow Jones company. It is a new record that surpasses the previous one from 2022, when Russia’s invasion of Ukraine sent energy markets into a tailspin.</p>','Business','[\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"World Politics\",\"Elections\",\"Small Business\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788612054956_img_1788612057487_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788612133702,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788612491098','Maria Bartiromo Out at Fox News','1788612491098','Network says the journalist is no longer with Fox News Media, effective Thursday','Fox News has parted ways with longtime anchor Maria Bartiromo. The journalist is no longer with Fox News Media, effective Thursday, the network said in a news r...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788612491098_img_1788612496395_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;</span>Fox News has parted ways with longtime anchor Maria Bartiromo.&nbsp;</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The journalist is no longer with Fox News Media, effective Thursday, the network said in a news release.</p>','World Politics','[\"CEOs & Executives\",\"Stocks\",\"Banking\",\"Jobs & Employment\",\"Tech\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788612491098_img_1788612496395_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788841024687,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788613042225','Volkswagen’s Peace Deal With Unions Sets Up Fresh Battles to Come','1788613042225','To win approval to cut thousands more jobs, automaker kicked questions about factory closures and governance down the road','To win approval to cut thousands more jobs, automaker kicked questions about factory closures and governance down the road','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788613042225_img_1788613045653_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;','World Politics','[\"Currencies\",\"Economy\",\"Interest Rates\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Innovation\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788613042225_img_1788613045653_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1788841086224,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788613358967','Computer Makers Are Selling Fewer PCs at Higher Prices. So Far, It’s Working','1788613358967','The trend is being driven by the shortage of memory chips, and accompanying soaring costs, stemming from the AI infrastructure buildout','Computer makers have been forced into an interesting trade off: Sell fewer PCs at far higher prices.The trend is being driven by the same shortage of memory chi...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788613358967_img_1788613361477_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\">&nbsp;</span>Computer makers have been forced into an interesting trade off: Sell fewer PCs at far higher prices.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The trend is being driven by the same shortage of memory chips, and accompanying soaring costs, stemming from the massive buildout of artificial-intelligence infrastructure. The bottleneck has trickled down to personal computers, which has sent prices higher, at the expense of units sold.</p><p class=\"css-16aepit e1jdulti0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; position: absolute; z-index: -1; top: 0px; left: -15000px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\">Copyright ©2026 Dow Jones &amp; Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. 87990cbe856818d5eddac44c7b1cdeb8</p><div class=\"css-nyleem e1hwu21o4\" style=\"clear: left; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\"></div><div class=\"css-1vlbiim-Container e1c45kzg0\" style=\"margin: 60px 0px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-family: Retina, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 17px;\"><div id=\"cx-snippet-overlay-container\" class=\"css-4tagk-SnippetOverlayContainer ewffk2a1\" style=\"position: relative; min-height: 210px; height: 405px;\"><div id=\"cx-snippet-overlay\" class=\"css-84wm0p-SnippetOverlay ewffk2a0\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0px; left: 0px; width: 620px; background-image: initial; background-position: initial; background-size: initial; background-repeat: initial; background-attachment: initial; background-origin: initial; background-clip: initial;\"><div class=\"tp-container-inner\" style=\"height: 405px; width: 620px;\"></div></div></div></div>','World Politics','[\"CEOs & Executives\",\"Stocks\",\"Jewelry\",\"Real Estate\",\"Crypto\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788613358967_img_1788613361477_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788839799879,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788613654374','Health Care Roundup: Market Talk','1788613654374','0207 ET – Hutchmed (China)’s deal with GSK appears to validate a specific drug candidate platform of the Hong Kong-based biopharmaceutical company before it enters clinical trials, say Citi analysts in a note.','Hutchmed entered an licensing deal with GSK that could be worth up to US$1.295 billion, excluding royalties on net sales, for a cancer drug. The deal, 1H sales ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788613654374_img_1788613657176_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\">&nbsp;Hutchmed entered an licensing deal with GSK that could be worth up to US$1.295 billion, excluding royalties on net sales, for a cancer drug. The deal, 1H sales momentum and a separate approval from Chinese regulators could materially improve visibility on Hutchmed’s guidance, they say, noting the company expects 2026 oncology and immunology revenue of US$330 million-US$450 million. Citi raises its 2026-2028 oncology and immunology revenue estimates by 14%-27%. The bank lifts its stock target price to 39.00 Hong Kong dollars from HK$36.00. Shares are up 3.3% at HK$22.60. (megan.cheah@wsj.com)</span>','World Politics','[\"Celebrity\",\"Upcoming Brands\",\"Architecture\",\"Manufacturing\",\"Culture\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788613654374_img_1788613657176_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788839833111,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788614814187','Lululemon Cuts Outlook Again After Another Tough Quarter for Sales','1788614814187','The activewear retailer says it now expects annual sales to be $10.35 billion to $10.5 billion, down from its previous guidance of $11 billion to $11.15 billion','Lululemon LULU -17.38%decrease; down pointing triangle Athletica cut its outlook for the second time this year following another quarter of declining sales in i...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788614814187_img_1788614817817_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<a data-type=\"company\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/LULU\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Lululemon</a><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif;\"> </span><a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/LULU\" class=\"css-1fr2kw9-ChicletStyle e1vl9ktx2\" style=\"position: relative; bottom: 3px; margin: 0px 5px; padding: 0px 0px 1px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16px; font-family: &quot;Retina Narrow&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 0.8px solid rgb(111, 111, 111);\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">LULU <span class=\"css-1hk2j0i-ChicletChange e1vl9ktx3\" style=\"display: inline-block; animation: 0.5s ease 0s 1 normal none running animation-1sre6o5; color: rgb(34, 34, 34);\">-17.38%</span></a><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\"><span style=\"display: unset;\"><a href=\"https://www.wsj.com/market-data/quotes/LULU\" class=\"css-1fr2kw9-ChicletStyle e1vl9ktx2\" style=\"position: relative; bottom: 3px; margin: 0px 5px; padding: 0px 0px 1px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: rgb(51, 51, 51); white-space: nowrap; text-decoration: none; cursor: pointer; font-size: 16px; font-family: &quot;Retina Narrow&quot;, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; border-bottom: 0.8px solid rgb(111, 111, 111);\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span class=\"css-1cwjurv-Arrow e1vl9ktx1\" style=\"margin-left: 3px;\"><span class=\"css-1q7p60h-ArrowHiddenLabel e1vl9ktx0\" style=\"position: absolute !important; width: 1px !important; height: 1px !important; padding: 0px !important; margin: -1px !important; overflow: hidden !important; clip: rect(0px, 0px, 0px, 0px) !important; border-style: none !important; border-color: currentcolor !important;\">decrease; down pointing triangle</span></span></a></span>&nbsp;Athletica cut its outlook for the second time this year following another quarter of declining sales in its Americas business.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u e1hwu21o0\" style=\"--summary-font-color: #555555; --summary-bullet-small-font-color: #222222; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); direction: ltr; font-family: Exchange, Georgia, serif; line-height: calc(1.55556); margin: 0px 0px 1em; overflow-wrap: break-word;\">The activewear retailer said Thursday it now expects annual sales to be $10.35 billion to $10.5 billion, down from its previous guidance of $11 billion to $11.15 billion. It also lowered its projection for earnings per share for the year to $9.48 to $9.73, down from $10.95 to $11.15.</p>','News','[\"Congress\",\"Business\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788614814187_img_1788614817817_0.webp',NULL,'[\"dfg\",\"sdfg\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1788837798559,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788616437664','Health Care Roundup: Market Talk','1788616437664','sdfg',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788616437664_img_1788616584981_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;erytuiu&nbsp; r6dtyui w','World Politics','[\"International News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Yapa',NULL,'Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788616437664_img_1788616584981_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788830122842,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788829680152','Jeju Police Officer Arrested After 298 Missing-Person Cases Come Under Scrutiny','1788829680152','A case involving two people later found dead has exposed a much wider problem, prompting authorities to review every missing-person report handled by the officer.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788829680152_img_1788829680225_0.webp\" alt=\"qw\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #475569; margin-right: 12px;\">qw</span><span style=\"font-size: 10px; font-family: monospace; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: ER)</span></div></figure><p style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>A missing-person case is supposed to trigger a search for answers. On South Korea\'s Jeju Island, authorities are now investigating how one police officer came to handle </span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\"><a href=\"https://en.yna.co.kr/view/AEN20260823000500315\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">298 missing-person reports</a></span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">, after allegations that he improperly closed cases without properly confirming that people were safe.</span></p><p style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 12pt 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; line-height: 1.38; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">The officer, identified by his surname </span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\"><a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/south-korea-missing-persons-jeju-island-police-06245925fbc7db3698482399d20cc9dc\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Bu</a></span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">, was arrested on </span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">August 25, 2026</span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">, on allegations including dereliction of duty, falsifying official electronic records and obstructing official duties. He has denied the allegations, although police said he later partially admitted to falsely telling the boyfriend of one missing woman that he had contacted her and confirmed she was safe.</span></p><p style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 12pt 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; line-height: 1.38; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">The scandal began to unravel after two missing-person cases handled by Bu were found to have been closed prematurely. One involved </span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">37-year-old Jang Mi-ran</span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">, who disappeared in May. Police later found a body believed to be hers on August 24, around </span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">104 days after she went missing</span><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">. Investigators found no call records supporting Bu\'s claim that he had spoken with her.</span></p><p style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 12pt 0px; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; line-height: 1.38; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-size: 11pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 0, 0); background-color: transparent; font-variant: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre-wrap; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">Another case involved a man in his 60s who had also been reported missing. His body was found after the case had allegedly been closed without proper confirmation of his safety.</span></p>','Business','[\"News\",\"Celebrity\",\"Architecture\",\"Books\",\"Entertainment\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','123','reader@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788829680152_img_1788829680225_0.webp',NULL,'[\"sd\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1788830041389,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1788830298058','Man Arrested Over Death of Former UK Politician Ann Widdecombe','1788830298058','A 28-year-old man has been arrested on suspicion of murdering former British politician Ann Widdecombe, according to police in England.','reform qww rjfbe The suspect, described by authorities as a white British national, was arrested on Saturday evening in South Yorkshire and remains in police cu...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_1788830298058_img_1788830301504_0.webp\" alt=\"reform qww rjfbe\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\" data-webp-converted=\"true\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #475569; margin-right: 12px;\">reform qww rjfbe </span></div></figure><p data-start=\"213\" data-end=\"400\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(26, 26, 26); font-family: &quot;Encorpada Classic Compressed Bold&quot;, &quot;Escrow Display Condensed Bold&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display Fallback&quot;, &quot;Playfair Display&quot;, Georgia, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>The suspect, described by authorities as a <span data-start=\"256\" data-end=\"282\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">white British national</span>, was arrested on Saturday evening in <span data-start=\"320\" data-end=\"339\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">South Yorkshire</span> and remains in police custody while investigations continue.<span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchor\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; line-height: 1.75 !important;\"></span></p><h3 data-section-id=\"2fj2ac\" data-start=\"402\" data-end=\"429\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">Investigation Continues</span></h3><p data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"545\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\">In a statement, <span data-start=\"447\" data-end=\"476\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">Devon and <a href=\"https://news.devon-cornwall.police.uk/news-article/3e2d22d4-787d-f111-9d98-6045bdd24049\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cornwall Police</a></span><a href=\"https://news.devon-cornwall.police.uk/news-article/3e2d22d4-787d-f111-9d98-6045bdd24049\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> confirmed</a> the arrest and said Widdecombe\'s family had been informed.</p><p data-start=\"547\" data-end=\"686\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\">The force also stated that officers were assisted by Counter Terrorism Policing North East and South Yorkshire Police during the operation.</p><p data-start=\"688\" data-end=\"774\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\">Investigators have said there is <span data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"746\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">currently no evidence</span> suggesting the killing was:</p><ul data-start=\"775\" data-end=\"820\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px 0px 1.25rem; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; font-size: 17px; text-align: justify;\"><li data-section-id=\"2ghlsz\" data-start=\"775\" data-end=\"796\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px 0px 0.5rem; padding: 0px; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">An act of terrorism</li><li data-section-id=\"1g1baw9\" data-start=\"797\" data-end=\"820\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px 0px 0.5rem; padding: 0px; line-height: 1.75 !important;\">Politically motivated</li></ul><h3 data-section-id=\"1d7u3pv\" data-start=\"822\" data-end=\"855\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">Widdecombe Found Dead at Home</span></h3><p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"939\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\">Widdecombe, 78, was discovered dead at her home in <span data-start=\"908\" data-end=\"925\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">Haytor, Devon</span>, on Thursday.</p><p data-start=\"941\" data-end=\"1038\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; padding: 0px; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-word; width: 916px; max-width: 100%; font-size: 17px; color: rgb(30, 41, 59); font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif;\">Police believe she died the previous day and reported that she had suffered <span data-start=\"1017\" data-end=\"1037\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; font-weight: bolder;\">serious injuries</span>.</p>','Business','[\"Law\",\"World Politics\",\"Elections\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1788830298058_img_1788830301504_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788830333799,'Sep 8, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032167433','US Sailors reach a Thai beach town after 250 Days at Sea and a War They Didn\'t Sign Up For.','1789032167433','The USS Abraham Lincoln departed from San Diego with six-months’ worth of mission time in the Pacific scheduled. Instead, it crashed in Iran and its 5,000-member crew has not come into contact with land for more than eight months.','The nuclear-powered aircraft carrier USS Abraham Lincoln has arrived off the coast of Thailand in Pattaya, about 250 days since it set sail without stopping a s...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032167433_img_1789032169747_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>The nuclear-powered aircraft carrier USS&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.washington-times.com/article/%EF%82%B7https://www.yahoo.com/news/us/articles/us-aircraft-carrier-dock-near-235952051.html\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Abraham Lincoln</a>&nbsp;has arrived off the coast of Thailand in Pattaya, about 250 days since it set sail without stopping a single port—finally, a respite for the ship\'s crew of nearly 5,000 sailors and Marines. It was supposed to be a routine 6-month assignment across the Pacific and South China Sea for the carrier, which left San Diego last November.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">So, what did keep it afloat for nearly 2000 years?</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">In war, and not that it was used for. The ship was diverted to the Gulf in the wake of US and Israeli military actions against Iran in late February, in which Admiral Cooper says the Lincoln dropped over 1.5 million pounds of weaponry and flew over 10,000 sorties. The situation on board allegedly deteriorated to the point where there were concerns to the Congress about food shortages, broken toilets and mental stress on the crew. The Navy acknowledged the deployment was difficult, but didn\'t elaborate on the Pattaya stop, citing \"<a href=\"https://www.scmp.com/week-asia/people/article/3365910/thailands-pattaya-pins-hopes-arrival-5000-us-sailors-boost-tourism\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">operational security</a>\".</p>','Business','[\"U.S. News\",\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"World Politics\",\"Elections\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032167433_img_1789032169747_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790157443771,'Sep 23, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032278831','Man Arrested in South Yorkshire Over Ann Widdecombe Murder Investigation','1789032278831','Haytor, Devon — Police investigating the murder of former British minister and Reform UK spokesperson Ann Widdecombe','Have arrested a 28-year-old man in South Yorkshire on suspicion of murder, marking a significant development in the high-profile investigation.Devon and Cornwal...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032278831_img_1789032280611_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Have arrested a 28-year-old man in South Yorkshire on suspicion of murder, marking a significant development in the high-profile investigation.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Devon and Cornwall Police confirmed that the suspect, described as a white British national, is currently being held in custody after officers carried out the arrest with assistance from Counter Terrorism Policing North East and South Yorkshire Police. Investigators stressed that there is no evidence indicating the killing was linked to terrorism or politically motivated.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Widdecombe, 78, was discovered with serious injuries at her home in Haytor, on the edge of Dartmoor National Park, at approximately 11:40 a.m. BST on Thursday. Detectives believe the fatal attack occurred nearly 24 hours before her body was found.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The latest arrest follows the release of a 26-year-old man who had initially been detained in nearby Newton Abbot. Police confirmed on Saturday that the individual had been eliminated from their inquiries and is no longer considered part of the investigation.</p>','International News','[\"Corporate News\",\"Entrepreneurship\",\"Markets & Finance\",\"Currencies\",\"Economy\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032278831_img_1789032280611_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1790612946634,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032358111','British Couple Seriously Injured After Being Trapped in Deadly Spain Wildfires','1789032358111','A British couple were rescued from a ravine in Spain\'s Almería province after becoming trapped in the devastating wildfires that have swept across the region, according to local reports.','The couple, believed to have been hiking when the fire spread rapidly through the area on Thursday, were discovered in critical condition by Civil Guard officer...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032358111_img_1789032360159_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>The couple, believed to have been hiking when the fire spread rapidly through the area on Thursday, were discovered in critical condition by Civil Guard officers conducting a search operation near the village of Bédar. Both suffered severe burns and were airlifted to hospital, where they remain in intensive care.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The wildfires have already claimed 12 lives, making them among the deadliest in Spain\'s recent history. Local authorities have reported that more than 6,600 hectares (16,300 acres) of land have been destroyed. While the identities of those who died have not yet been officially confirmed, reports suggest that four of the victims may have been British nationals.</p><h2>Dramatic Rescue</h2><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The couple were found in the early hours of Friday after rescuers heard faint cries for help coming from a steep ravine.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\"><a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cx2x7441762o\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\"As you gain more experience,</a>&nbsp;something inside you tells you, \'Look again, try one more time,\'\" Civil Guard Sergeant Pedro Barre told Spanish broadcaster TVE.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Following the sound, officers climbed down the hillside and located the pair. Rescue officials said both victims were semi-conscious and had burns covering approximately 40% of their bodies.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">\"Being able to call out in the condition they were in was a titanic effort,\" said rescuer Rafael Zea.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Barre added: \"We\'ll never forget the look of surprise and emotion on their faces.\"</p><h2>Fire Situation Improving</h2><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Emergency services have continued containment and recovery operations across the affected region. On Sunday, Andalusian regional president Juan Manuel Moreno Bonilla announced that the wildfire had been contained and its perimeter secured, allowing authorities to lower the emergency alert level.</p>','Law','[\"Interest Rates\",\"Artificial Intelligence\",\"Innovation\",\"Movies\",\"Music\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032358111_img_1789032360159_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790603479176,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032442811','Jonathan Meléndez: A Brutal Crime That Has Shocked Mexico','1789032442811','The murder of the Camilo Séptimo musician, his pregnant wife, their young daughter and a domestic worker has reignited concerns about violence, criminality and insecurity in Mexico.','Mexico\'s music community has been shaken by the murder of Jonathan Samuel Meléndez Ochoa, known professionally as “Honas,” a 38-year-old keyboardist, composer a...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032442811_img_1789032444386_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Mexico\'s music community has been shaken by the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/media-telecom/mexican-musician-family-members-slain-gruesome-shooting-upscale-penthouse-2026-09-02/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">murder</a>&nbsp;of&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"305\" data-end=\"339\">Jonathan Samuel Meléndez Ochoa</strong>, known professionally as “Honas,” a 38-year-old keyboardist, composer and producer and one of the founding members of the alternative band&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"479\" data-end=\"497\">Camilo Séptimo</strong>. Meléndez was killed alongside his wife, their three-year-old daughter and a 21-year-old domestic worker inside the family\'s apartment in Atizapán de Zaragoza, State of Mexico.</p><p data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"1115\">The&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.nmas.com.mx/seguridad/asesinatos/que-paso-jonathan-melendez-claves-homicidio-tecladista-camilo-septimo-atizapan/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">attack</a>&nbsp;occurred on September 1 in the Grand Viure residential complex in the Bosque Esmeralda area. According to the State of Mexico prosecutor\'s office, the victims were found after neighbors reported screams and possible gunshots. Two of the victims had been restrained, while the victims suffered fatal gunshot wounds. The family\'s dog was also found dead.<span class=\"contents\" data-content-reference-start=\"1072\" data-content-reference-end=\"1104\"><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span></span></p><p data-start=\"1117\" data-end=\"1323\">Meléndez\'s wife, Ana Paola, was pregnant at the time of the attack. Their six-year-old son survived after hiding inside the apartment and was found physically unharmed. The brutality of the crime has generated particular outrage because the victims were apparently targeted inside their own home, in a residential area considered relatively secure.</p><p data-start=\"1539\" data-end=\"1843\">Investigators have arrested two men in connection with the killings. One of them,&nbsp;<a href=\"https://elpais.com/mexico/2026-09-04/diego-sebastian-rosen-ferlini-y-el-dia-despues-del-crimen-contra-un-pais.html?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Diego Sebastián</a>&nbsp;“N,” was a business associate of Meléndez. Authorities are investigating whether financial disagreements connected to a property-rental business were behind the attack. However,&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1854\" data-end=\"1910\">the motive has not yet been definitively established</strong>, and the suspects remain legally presumed innocent. Mexican authorities continue investigating the circumstances surrounding the crime. The fact that one suspect allegedly knew Meléndez is particularly significant. Investigators believe that his relationship with the musician may have allowed him to enter the residence without immediately raising suspicion.</p>','News','[\"Arts\",\"Architecture\",\"Culture\",\"Energy\",\"Manufacturing\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032442811_img_1789032444386_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790603470431,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032520790','Peter Cullen, the Legendary Voice of Optimus Prime and Eeyore, Dies at 85','1789032520790','The legendary Canadian voice actor gave life to Optimus Prime, Eeyore and dozens of other memorable characters across a career spanning more than five decades.','For generations of fans, Optimus Prime had a voice. Now, that voice has fallen silent.Peter Cullen, the acclaimed Canadian voice actor best known for portraying...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032520790_img_1789032522856_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>For generations of fans, Optimus Prime had a voice. Now, that voice has fallen silent.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/movies/movie-news/peter-cullen-optimus-prime-transformers-eeyore-1236683075/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Peter Cullen</a>, the acclaimed Canadian voice actor best known for portraying the heroic leader of the Autobots in Transformers, has died at the age of 85. Cullen died on August 26 at his home in Los Angeles, surrounded by his family, according to his agent and family. His cause of death has not been disclosed. </p><p>Cullen first became the voice of Optimus Prime in the original 1984 animated Transformers series, establishing the deep, authoritative voice that would become inseparable from the character. He later returned to the role across animated productions, video games and Michael Bay’s live-action Transformers films.</p><p>His portrayal of <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2026/aug/27/actor-peter-cullen-voice-optimus-prime-and-eeyore-dies\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Optimus Prime</a> was more than simply a distinctive voice. Cullen helped shape the character as a leader defined by strength, compassion and responsibility. He drew inspiration for the character\'s voice from his brother Larry, a Vietnam War veteran and former U.S. Marine. </p><p>But Optimus Prime was only one part of Cullen’s extraordinary career.</p><p>He was also widely recognized as Eeyore in Disney’s Winnie the Pooh productions, bringing his famously deep voice to the gloomy but beloved donkey. His other credits included KARR in Knight Rider, King Kong in the 1976 film and the vocal effects for the Predator in the 1987 science-fiction action movie.&nbsp;</p>','International News','[\"Construction\",\"Designers\",\"Investing\",\"Wealth Management\",\"Health\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032520790_img_1789032522856_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790603457121,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032604541','Why Do Hot Springs Really Get Hot? The Solution Begins Far Below Your Feet','1789032604541','There is absolutely no heat at the beginning of the bubbling water. On a long, deep detour, it is rainfall.','With no stove or fire in sight, the water rising directly out of the ground and already steaming appears almost miraculous. The true explanation begins far earl...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032604541_img_1789032606456_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>With no stove or fire in sight, the water rising directly out of the ground and already&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/media/images/hot-springs-alaska-caused-geothermal-activity-underground\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 12pt;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">steaming</a>&nbsp;appears almost miraculous. The true explanation begins far earlier than most people realize and much below the surface. Before it ever reappears as something you would like to swim in, the majority of hot springs start out as perfectly normal rain or groundwater that seeps through fissures and faults in the Earth\'s crust, often for years.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">What, then, heats it during the process? Depending on the location, there are two primary routes. Groundwater can come into direct touch with shallow pockets of magma, or molten rock that is relatively close to the surface, in areas where volcanism is active. This causes the water to heat up significantly as it goes by. In locations without volcanic activity, heat is generated by something slower and more consistent: the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/news/featured-story/its-a-hot-topic-geothermal-energy-and-how-usgs-science-could-help-harness-it\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">geothermal&nbsp;</a>gradient, which is simply the fact that rock temperature rises as you go deeper beneath. When water seeps far enough, it finally comes into contact with rock that is hot enough to warm it without the need for magma.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The water does not stay down there either way. When heated, it loses density relative to the surrounding cooler water, which causes it to rise through fissures and cracks until it eventually emerges as a hot spring. A hot spring can become a geyser by periodically erupting if the underground plumbing system is precisely constructed to hold pressure until it bursts abruptly.</p>','U.S. News','[\"Health\",\"Soccer\",\"Mental Health\",\"Tennis\",\"Lifestyle\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032604541_img_1789032606456_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790579092449,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032673440','Venezuela’s Transition Is Moving. But Too Slowly to Solve the Country’s Immediate Problems','1789032673440','Judicial reforms, political prisoner releases and economic reopening show real progress, but millions of Venezuelans are still waiting for concrete improvements in their daily lives','Venezuela\'s post-Maduro transition has produced several important developments in 2026, but the process remains considerably slower than the urgency of the coun...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032673440_img_1789032675104_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Venezuela\'s post-Maduro transition has produced several important developments in 2026, but the process remains considerably slower than the urgency of the country\'s problems demands.</p><p data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"995\">The first major achievement has been the opening of formal&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/longform/2026/8/14/talks-between-government-and-opposition-mark-a-new-chapter-for-venezuela?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">negotiations</a>&nbsp;between the government of interim President&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"583\" data-end=\"602\">Delcy Rodríguez</strong>&nbsp;and part of the opposition. The first round concluded in August with an agreement to begin transforming the judicial system, including the replacement of the Supreme Tribunal\'s magistrates through a new selection process. The sides also agreed to seek access to Venezuelan reserves frozen in the Bank of England to help finance earthquake reconstruction.<span class=\"contents\" data-content-reference-start=\"958\" data-content-reference-end=\"988\"><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span></span></p><p data-start=\"997\" data-end=\"1336\">These are significant steps. Venezuela\'s judiciary has long been criticized for its dependence on the executive, and the Supreme Tribunal validated Nicolás Maduro\'s disputed 2024 electoral victory. Reforming that institution could therefore become one of the foundations of a future democratic system.<span class=\"contents\" data-content-reference-start=\"1292\" data-content-reference-end=\"1309\"><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span></span></p><p data-start=\"1338\" data-end=\"1713\">There has also been movement on political prisoners. An amnesty law approved in February facilitated the release of hundreds of detainees, while Rodríguez announced another 131 releases in August. Yet human-rights organizations reported that&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1580\" data-end=\"1612\">hundreds remained imprisoned</strong>, and many released individuals continued to face restrictions.</p>','Politics','[\"Food & Dining\",\"Science\",\"Climate\",\"Research\",\"Editorials\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032673440_img_1789032675104_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',1,1790574997052,'Sep 28, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032745588','Alejandro Betancourt: The Controversial Oilman at the Center of Trump’s Venezuela Strategy','1789032745588','A businessman investigated for alleged corruption and money laundering has become a key intermediary between Washington and Delcy Rodríguez, raising questions about who is really benefiting from Venezuela’s oil reopening','Venezuela\'s oil industry is undergoing one of the most dramatic transformations in decades. Under the Trump administration, Washington is pushing to reopen the ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032745588_img_1789032747495_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Venezuela\'s oil industry is undergoing one of the most dramatic transformations in decades. Under the Trump administration, Washington is pushing to reopen the country\'s enormous energy sector to American investment. But at the center of this process is a controversial Venezuelan businessman:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.bloomberglinea.com/latinoamerica/venezuela/el-magnate-detras-de-la-nueva-apuesta-de-trump-por-el-petroleo-venezolano/?_=RANDOM&amp;reader_id=READER_ID&amp;url=SOURCE_URL&amp;utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><strong data-start=\"614\" data-end=\"638\">Alejandro Betancourt</strong>.</a></p><p data-start=\"641\" data-end=\"994\">Betancourt has become an important intermediary between the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/world/trumps-powerful-unofficial-venezuela-adviser-leaves-his-role-2026-07-31/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Trump administration</a>&nbsp;and the government of Delcy Rodríguez. Former Trump adviser Mauricio Claver-Carone acknowledged that U.S. officials used Betancourt because he understood both the Venezuelan and American oil industries and could connect the two sides. The controversy comes from Betancourt\'s past.</p><p data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1418\">He became wealthy during the Chávez era through Derwick Associates, a company that obtained billions of dollars in Venezuelan energy contracts. Transparency International previously estimated that Derwick\'s contracts involved approximately&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1283\" data-end=\"1322\">$2.9 billion in alleged overbilling</strong>, allegations that Betancourt and the company have denied.<span class=\"contents\" data-content-reference-start=\"1374\" data-content-reference-end=\"1404\"><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span><span class=\"\" data-state=\"closed\"></span></span></p><p data-start=\"1420\" data-end=\"1925\">More seriously, Betancourt is currently under&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.thetimes.com/world/latin-america/article/venezuelan-oil-man-investigated-overseas-is-key-broker-for-trump-pv0kbjt6m?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">investigation</a>&nbsp;in Spain and Switzerland over alleged money laundering, tax fraud and corruption connected to Venezuelan oil operations. Spanish authorities reopened a case in June involving allegations that $42 million in bribes were paid to Venezuelan state-oil officials as part of a scheme involving billions of dollars in currency transactions.&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"1814\" data-end=\"1887\">Betancourt denies wrongdoing and has never been convicted of a crime.&nbsp;</strong>Yet despite these investigations, his influence over Venezuela\'s oil sector has increased.</p>','World Politics','[\"News\",\"U.S. News\",\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"Congress\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032745588_img_1789032747495_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790518015045,'Sep 27, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789032821715','Why Do We Procrastinate Even When We know Better?','1789032821715','You are aware that the deadline is nearing and that the work must be completed. Suddenly, checking your phone, watching a video or doing something completely different becomes much easier. Why is it that we love to put things off?','Procrastination is frequently viewed as laziness, but there is more to the psychology of procrastination. It is defined by researchers as needlessly postponing ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\">&nbsp;<img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032821715_img_1789032823625_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Procrastination is frequently viewed as laziness, but there is more to the psychology of procrastination. It is defined by researchers as needlessly postponing a desired action when there is a potential for harm. Research is becoming more and more associated with the link between procrastination and emotion regulation. Sometimes, we don\'t want to do something because we don\'t want the feeling we get from the result rather than the action itself.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Think of arriving at an assignment and being overwhelmed by it. You don\'t start, instead you look at social media. This is a short-term discomfort that lasts for a few minutes. That temporary relief can reinforce the habit, making it easier to repeat the behaviour later.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Even clues could be found within the brain. An MRI study published in Psychological Science in 2018 identified the amygdala as a brain area that is associated with procrastination. The people with less action control had a larger amygdala and weaker links between the amygdala and the dorsal anterior cingulate cortex, which is part of the brain that controls actions.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">But that doesn\'t mean that a bigger amygdala leads to procrastination. The study found an association, but not a direct cause, and more research is required to understand the mechanisms in the brain, researchers said.</p>','U.S. News','[\"Personal Finance\",\"Opinion\",\"Environment\",\"Space\",\"Cars\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789032821715_img_1789032823625_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[\"kitty\",\"black\"]','5 min read',0,1790646946238,'Sep 29, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"ishmithabimsarani@gmail.com\"]',1,'We We','Why Do We Procrastinate Even When We know Better?','Procrastination is frequently viewed as laziness, but there is more to the psychology of procrastination. It is defined by researchers as needlessly postponing','[]'),('1789088719027','Amelia Dimoldenberg Is Closing the Chicken Shop After 12 Years','1789088719027','After turning awkward celebrity interviews over fried chicken into one of YouTube\'s most recognizable formats, Amelia Dimoldenberg has announced that Chicken Shop Date is coming to an end.','One of the internet\'s most awkward and somehow most successful love stories is coming to an end.Amelia Dimoldenberg has announced that her hit YouTube series, C...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789088719027_img_1789088720986_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>One of the internet\'s most awkward and somehow most successful love stories is coming to an end.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/celebrity/articles/amelia-dimoldenberg-ending-chicken-shop-144551945.html\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Amelia Dimoldenberg</a> has announced that her hit YouTube series, Chicken Shop Date, will end after 12 years, closing the chapter on a show that transformed uncomfortable silences, deadpan flirting and fried chicken into a global entertainment phenomenon.</p><p>Dimoldenberg announced the news in an emotional message shared on social media, telling fans that she felt it was time to leave the long-running series behind and begin something new.</p><p>“I feel like it’s now time to move on from this adventure and onto a new one,” she wrote.</p><p>For those unfamiliar with the show, <a href=\"https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/a73643988/chicken-shop-date-amelia-dimoldenberg-snl-uk/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Chicken Shop Date</a> was never a typical celebrity interview.</p><p>Dimoldenberg would take musicians, actors, athletes and internet personalities on deliberately awkward “dates” inside chicken shops, combining flirting, uncomfortable pauses and hilariously blunt questions. What began as a small project eventually became one of YouTube\'s most recognizable interview formats.</p><p>The series began in 2014, initially featuring figures from the British grime and music scene before growing into an international phenomenon. Over the years, Dimoldenberg sat across the table from some of the biggest names in entertainment, including Andrew Garfield, Billie Eilish, Jennifer Lawrence, Paul McCartney, Sabrina Carpenter, Cher and Cynthia Erivo.</p><p>But perhaps the show\'s biggest strength was that no celebrity could completely escape Amelia\'s interview style.</p><p>Whether she was pretending not to understand something a guest said, awkwardly flirting with them or simply staring into the camera after an uncomfortable answer, Dimoldenberg created a format that felt completely different from traditional talk shows.</p><p>Her interviews regularly went viral, turning Chicken Shop Date from a niche online series into a major part of internet pop culture.</p>','Culture','[\"Music\",\"Television\",\"Celebrity\",\"Movies\",\"Arts\"]','Home - Main Bottom Panel','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789088719027_img_1789088720986_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789299811631,'Sep 13, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789131167596','Elon Musk’s xAI Fails to Block Minnesota’s AI Nudification Ban','1789131167596','A federal judge has refused to halt Minnesota\'s first-of-its-kind law targeting AI tools used to create nonconsensual fake nude images, allowing the ban to remain in effect as xAI\'s legal challenge continues.','Elon Musk\'s artificial intelligence company xAI has lost its latest attempt to block Minnesota\'s ban on AI “nudification” technology.A federal judge ruled on Se...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789131167596_img_1789131169674_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Elon Musk\'s artificial intelligence company xAI has lost its latest attempt to block Minnesota\'s ban on AI “nudification” technology.</p><p>A federal judge ruled on <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/legal/litigation/musks-xai-loses-court-bid-block-minnesotas-ai-nudification-ban-2026-09-04/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">September 4, 2026</a>, that Minnesota\'s law can remain in effect while xAI\'s constitutional challenge continues through the courts. The company had asked for a preliminary injunction that would have temporarily stopped enforcement of the law. </p><p>The law is broader than simply a ban on AI-generated child sexual abuse material.</p><p>Minnesota\'s legislation specifically targets <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/minnesota/news/ai-nudification-musk-lawsuit-judge-rules-injunction/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">AI technology</a> that can digitally alter images of real, identifiable people to make them appear nude or create sexual imagery without their consent. Supporters say the measure is intended to address the growing misuse of generative AI, including the creation of sexualized images involving children. </p><p>The law officially took effect on August 1, 2026, making Minnesota the first U.S. state to enact such a statewide ban on AI “nudification” technology.</p><p>xAI, the company behind Musk\'s AI chatbot Grok, filed its lawsuit against Minnesota before the law took effect.</p><p>The company argued that the legislation violated constitutional protections for free speech and claimed it could force xAI to restrict certain features of its technology for users in the state. </p><p>But U.S. District Judge Donovan Frank declined to grant xAI\'s request to block t</p>','Tech','[\"Elections\",\"Legal Affairs\"]','Home- In Depth Panel','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Trash','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789131167596_img_1789131169674_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789131191946,'Sep 11, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789657863931','Young Streamer Gtwist\'s Viral Family Confrontation Sparks Safety Debate','1789657863931','A disturbing clip from the young Kick streamer\'s August 30 broadcast has triggered widespread concern, while key details about what happened remain unverified.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 100%; clear: left; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789657863931_img_1789657866220_0.webp\" alt=\"qwe\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #64748b; margin-right: 12px;\">qwe</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-size: 10px; font-weight: bold; font-family: monospace, sans-serif; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: QWE)</span></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Young streamer <a href=\"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us-streamers/what-happened-to-kick-streamer-gtwist-livestream-clip-sparks-debate-after-alleged-confrontation-with-his-father/articleshow/133636562.cms\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Gtwist</a> has become the center of a major online debate after a distressing clip from his livestream spread widely across social media on August 30, 2026.</p><p>The approximately two-minute video appears to show an adult man entering Gtwist\'s room during a livestream and physically confronting him before the streamer becomes visibly upset and ends the broadcast. Reports and social media users have identified the man as a member of his family, although details surrounding their relationship have been disputed online. </p><p>The clip quickly sparked concern among viewers because Gtwist is widely described online as a young streamer, with some posts claiming he is a minor. However, his exact age has not been independently confirmed, according to available reporting. </p><p>During the broadcast, Gtwist appeared increasingly distressed before the stream abruptly ended.</p><p>The incident also drew attention because Gtwist has previously sha</p>','World Politics','[\"International News\",\"News\",\"Criminal Cases\",\"Politics\",\"Elections\"]','Home - A+ Main News','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789657863931_img_1789657866220_0.webp',NULL,'[\"qwe\"]','[]','5 min read',10,1789657957638,'Sep 17, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 14:40:02','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789659946287','sdf','1789659946287','fghj','sdfgha vygyggiy','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789659946287_img_1789659949624_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<a href=\"https://\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\">sdfgha </a>vygyggiy&nbsp;','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789659946287_img_1789659949624_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789659962063,'Sep 17, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789666471891','Wrong Drug Given During Surgeries Leaves Nashville Patients With Severe Injuries','1789666471891','A medication mix-up at Ascension Saint Thomas Midtown left at least one patient paralyzed, while Tennessee authorities investigate how the error happened.','At least four patients were harmed after receiving the wrong medication during routine joint replacement surgeries at Ascension Saint Thomas Midtown Hospital in...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789666471891_img_1789666474138_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>At least <a href=\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/nashville-hospital-drug-mix-up-complications/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">four patients</a> were harmed after <a href=\"https://sdfg.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\">receiving </a>the wrong medication during routine joint replacement surgeries at Ascension Saint Thomas Midtown Hospital in Nashville, Tennessee, on August 14.</p><p>According to CBS News and local reports, the patients were supposed to receive medication used for pain control through an epidural. Instead, they were given a potassium-based <a href=\"https://asd\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\">medication</a>. One patient, 72-year-old Glenda Dorton, was <a href=\"https://www.wsmv.com/video/2026/08/20/nashville-patient-left-paralyzed-after-drug-mix-up-family-says/\" style=\"border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-weight: 600;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">left paralyzed</a> from the chest down, according to her family.</p><p>Dorton had gone to the hospital for what was expected to be a routine knee replacement. Her family said the surgery itself went well, but the medication error left her in intensive care as doctors assess whether her condition can improve.</p><p>The hospital initially described the incident as an “event” involving four patients. It later confirmed that the medication error occurred in the hospital pharmacy and said the <a href=\"https://\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" style=\"color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\">patients </a>received potassium phosphate instead of the intended anesthetic.</p><p>The exact circumstances behind the mix-up are still being investigated. The Tennessee Bureau of Investigation is now involved, while the hospital has reported the incident to state regulators.</p>','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789666471891_img_1789666474138_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789666515495,'Sep 17, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1789667916019','qwertyu','1789667916019','asdfgj','sdfgh fnjef ajndjd ah a','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789667916019_img_1789667918205_0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;sdfgh <a href=\"https://qe.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#111111] font-semibold underline\" style=\"color: rgb(17, 17, 17); font-weight: 600; text-decoration: underline;\">fnjef</a> ajndjd ah a','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1789667916019_img_1789667918205_0.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1789667928292,'Sep 17, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790295575455','What is the reason that some cultures feed their newborns with something sweet?','1790295575455','The birth of a baby has been celebrated with rites to express sweetness, blessings and wishes for a healthy life from Islamic Tahneek to birth rituals in Hindu and Sikh faith. Interestingly, modern medicine also uses a form of sugar to help some newborn babies maintain their healthy blood glucose levels','qwer(PHOTO: QWER) One of these traditions is Tahneek, a Muslim ritual that involves rubbing a soft date in the palate (mouth) of the newborn. It is narrated in ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790295575455_img_1790295578029_0.webp\" alt=\"qwer\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #64748b; margin-right: 12px;\">qwer</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-size: 10px; font-weight: bold; font-family: monospace, sans-serif; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: QWER)</span></div></figure><div><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>One of these traditions is Tahneek, a Muslim ritual that involves rubbing a soft date in the palate (mouth) of the newborn. It is narrated in several hadiths. In the book of Sahih Muslim, it is recorded that the children were brought to the Holy Prophet (Saws) when they were born, he blessed them and performed <a href=\"https://www.cochrane.org/evidence/CD011027_oral-dextrose-gel-treatment-newborn-infants-low-blood-glucose-levels\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Tahneek</a> with dates.</div><div>The practice is considered as a Sunnah and is followed by Muslim families for centuries. However, there is an interesting question to consider when we examine the concept across other religious traditions.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>Why is it that the idea of giving a baby something sweet is found in multiple cultures?</div><div><br></div><div>Within Hindu tradition, a small amount of ghee and honey has been offered to newborns during the ancient Jatakarma birth ceremony, and prayers have been recited to bestow intelligence, long life and other qualities.</div><div>Sweetness is also involved in some of the ceremonies of the newborn children for the Sikhs. About the naming ceremony it states that a drop of honey may be given to the baby\'s mouth and prayers recited and the naming ceremony later held at the gurdwara.</div><div><br></div><div>The subject has another interesting link with modern medicine.</div><div><br></div><div>Following birth, it is important that newborn infants rapidly make the transition from placental glucose to self-maintenance of blood glucose levels. There is a risk of neonatal hypoglycemia (low blood glucose) in some babies, especially premature babies, low-birth-weight infants, those born to mothers with diabetes.</div>','News','[\"U.S. News\",\"World Politics\",\"Congress\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790295575455_img_1790295578029_0.webp',NULL,'[\"ert\",\"qwe\",\"asdf\",\"cv\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790305988433,'Sep 25, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"plm@gmail.com\",\"okn@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790296303327','Solar Train turns sunshine into movement in Argentina.','1790296303327','Sunlight is shining more than just on the Andes in the high, plateaus of northern Argentina. It is assisting to power a train that is running through one of the most stunning landscapes in South America.','Solar train turns(PHOTO: GETTY IMAGES) The Tren Solar de la Quebrada is a 42-kilometre long train that traverses the Quebrada de Humahuaca, a UNESCO World Herit...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790296303327_img_1790296305490_0.webp\" alt=\"Solar train turns\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #64748b; margin-right: 12px;\">Solar train turns</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-size: 10px; font-weight: bold; font-family: monospace, sans-serif; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: GETTY IMAGES)</span></div></figure><div><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>The Tren Solar de la Quebrada is a 42-kilometre long train that traverses the Quebrada de Humahuaca, a <a href=\"https://www.euronews.com/2026/09/20/argentinas-first-solar-train-runs-on-batteries-charged-by-the-andean-sun\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">UNESCO</a> World Heritage listed valley that has been a vital route along the Andes Mountains for thousands of years. The train runs between 6 towns, including Volcán, Purmamarca and Tilcara.</div><div><br></div><div>The train\'s name is misleading as there are no solar panels on the roof. On the contrary, it has to use six lithium batteries to move its two carriages, and solar electricity is produced locally in Jujuy to charge them.</div><div><br></div><div>Some energy is also recovered on applying brake the train. That energy is stored in the batteries, and can later be used to assist in powering the train.</div><div><br></div><div>The power of a railway in a different way.</div><div><br></div><div>So, what is the maximum possible range for a train to be able to run with this?</div><div><br></div><div>The batteries have a range of between 100 and 120 kilometres; that\'s double the length of the 42 kilometre train\'s current route, the operator said. The train is able to charge at high speed at both Volcán and <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20260710-ride-argentinas-first-solar-train-through-10000-years-of-indigenous-history\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Purmamarca</a>.</div><div>The project is significant for reasons other than technology. In 2024, passenger transport was reintroduced to the Quebrada de Humahuaca with the solar train. The Jujuy government reports that over 90,000 passengers have so far used the service since it opened.</div><div><br></div><div>The train also forms part of a broader trend towards cleaner train traffic. Many electric trains use overhead power lines, but battery trains don\'t require them; they could be useful where there\'s not enough room to put the power lines up.</div><div><br></div><div>The solar train of <a href=\"https://electrek.co/2026/08/03/argentinas-solar-train-brings-zero-emission-travel-to-an-ancient-trade-route/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Argentina</a> is a unique case in which solar power is being used in a different way to suit local requirements. In a region where sunshine is abundant, the same sunlight illuminating the Andes is helping move people through them.</div>','Business','[\"International News\",\"Politics\",\"World Politics\",\"Law\",\"Space\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790296303327_img_1790296305490_0.webp',NULL,'[\"dfghj\",\"sdfghjk\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790305069085,'Sep 25, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"ljh@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790299086921','Lebanese Journalist Wounded After Strike Hits During Live Broadcast','1790299086921','Al-Manar correspondent Ali Chbib and cameraman Mohammad Berjawi were reportedly wounded when a strike hit nearby as they prepared for a live broadcast in southern Lebanon',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790299086921_img_1790299087168_0.webp\" alt=\"Al-Manar\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"margin-right: 12px;\">Al-Manar</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-family: monospace, sans-serif; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: GETTY IMAGES)</span></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>A <a href=\"https://newscord.org/article/israeli-forces-strike-south-lebanon-shelling-ali-al-taher-heights-with-phosphoru--Story_20260816_IsraelstrikessouthLec42dc5e3\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">live television</a> report from southern Lebanon was suddenly interrupted when an Israeli strike hit near a journalist preparing to go on air.</p><p><a href=\"https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/caught-on-cam-strike-hits-close-to-reporter-live-on-air-in-lebanon/articleshow/133958355.cms\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Al-Manar</a> correspondent Ali Chbib and cameraman Mohammad Berjawi were wounded in the incident on September 6 in Nabatieh al-Fawqa, a town in southern Lebanon, according to their broadcaster. Video from the channel captured Chbib preparing for the report before a blast struck nearby, sending smoke and debris through the area and cutting the live feed.</p><p>The incident came as Israeli strikes continued across southern Lebanon despite a U.S.-brokered ceasefire with Hezbollah agreed in June. Israel has continued military operations in parts of southern Lebanon, saying its strikes are aimed at Hezbollah positions and weapons facilities.</p><p>The Israeli military said it had carried out strikes in the Nabatieh area after what it described as attacks by Hezbollah involving explosive drones. The military said it targeted Hezbollah fighters and facilities and maintained that it does not intentionally target journalists or other uninvolved people.</p>','Business','[\"Criminal Cases\",\"Politics\",\"Markets & Finance\",\"Currencies\",\"Artificial Intelligence\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790299086921_img_1790299087168_0.webp',NULL,'[\"qwe\",\"rtyy\",\"hjk\",\"fh\",\"dfg\"]','[\"lebanese\",\"journal\",\"hits\",\"during\"]','5 min read',0,1790305002436,'Sep 25, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:05','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"zxc@gmail.com\",\"sdf@gmail.com\"]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790327276247','The Education Legacy That Still Shapes Sri Lankan Children Today','1790327276247','Each morning thousands of Sri Lankan children walk into classrooms carrying a chance to their classrooms that was once denied to much of the nation\'s population. There is a reform behind that opportunity, which is changing the direction of education in Sri Lanka','qwertyuiop(PHOTO: GETTY) Dr. C. W. W. Kannangara, popularly known as the Father of Free Education, was a key figure in the development of Sri Lanka\'s education ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790327276247_img_1790327279184_0.webp\" alt=\"qwertyuiop\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"margin-right: 12px;\">qwertyuiop</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-family: monospace, sans-serif; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: GETTY)</span></div></figure>&nbsp;<div>Dr. C. W. W. Kannangara, popularly known as the Father of Free Education, was a key figure in the development of Sri Lanka\'s education system. His efforts contributed to the development of a system that allows children to be educated regardless of their family\'s means. The sweeping changes took effect on 1 October 1945.</div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/posts/the-day-news-global_thedaynewsglobal-tdng-cwwkannangara-activity-7507829494720892929-nGRD\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kannangara\'s</a> efforts did not stop at the school fees. The reforms were also designed to increase educational opportunities for children outside the nation\'s big cities. Central Schools were created in rural regions and talented children from poorer families were able to attend via scholarship and boarding.</div><div><br></div><div>A Legacy that can still be seen in Today\'s Classrooms</div><div><br></div><div>How can a reform that’s been in place for over 80 years impact a child in a classroom?</div><div><br></div><div>Quite a lot.</div><div><br></div><div>A child in a rural family can get an education, take national exams, go to university and become a doctor, engineer, teacher, researcher, or professional, regardless of his or her family\'s income.</div>','Business','[\"News\",\"International News\",\"Criminal Cases\",\"Congress\",\"Politics\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_1790327276247_img_1790327279184_0.webp',NULL,'[\"zx\",\"cv\",\"bn\"]','[\"qwe\",\"tyu\",\"uio\"]','5 min read',0,1790327342194,'Sep 25, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:04','2026-10-20 08:00:00','[\"qwe@gmail.com\",\"asd@gmail.com\"]',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790772177856','Harvey Weinstein Sentenced to 15 Years for 2006 Sexual Assault','1790772177856','The former Hollywood producer was sentenced after being convicted again of sexually assaulting former production assistant Miriam Haley, years after his original New York conviction was overturned.','Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday after a New York jury convicted him of sexually assaulting former production assistant Miriam Hal...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772147755.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span><a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/news/us-news/harvey-weinstein-sentenced-15-years-new-york-sex-crime-conviction-rcna599213\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Harvey Weinstein</a> was sentenced to <a href=\"https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260923-disgraced-hollywood-mogul-harvey-weinstein-sentenced-to-15-years-for-2006-sex-assault\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">15 years</a> in prison Wednesday after a New York jury convicted him of sexually assaulting former production assistant Miriam Haley in 2006. The sentence marks another chapter in the former Hollywood producer\'s long-running criminal case, which has gone through multiple trials and appeals. </p><p>Weinstein, 74, appeared in a Manhattan courtroom in a wheelchair for the sentencing. Prosecutors had asked for 20 years, while his defense requested a nine-year sentence, citing his age and health problems. </p><p>Haley addressed the court before the sentence was announced, describing the lasting effects of the assault and the years of legal proceedings that followed. She said the experience had affected her sense of safety and described the consequences as continuing long after the 2006 incident. </p><p>Weinstein expressed regret for the pain Haley said she experienced but continued to maintain his innocence regarding the assault. He asked the judge for mercy and said he was not a perfect person but had made mistakes. </p><p>The latest sentence follows a complicated legal history. Weinstein was originally convicted in New York in 2020 and sentenced to 23 years after being found guilty of sexually assaulting Haley and raping aspiring actress Jessica Mann. New York\'s highest court overturned those convictions in 2024, ruling that the original trial had been unfair because of testimony concerning allegations that were not part of the charges.</p>','U.S. News','[\"News\",\"Law\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"World Politics\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772147755.webp',NULL,'[\"qwer\",\"dfg\"]','[\"qwe\"]','5 min read',0,1790772305338,'Sep 30, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Harvey Weinstein Sentenced Years','Harvey Weinstein Sentenced to 15 Years for 2006 Sexual Assault','Harvey Weinstein was sentenced to 15 years in prison Wednesday after a New York jury convicted him of sexually assaulting former production assistant Miriam Hal','[]'),('1790772493800','Radio signals have been detected directly from an exoplanet.','1790772493800','Astronomers have uncovered radio waves they claim can be directly linked to a planet outside our Solar System for the first time, which will provide a new means for astronomers to explore worlds beyond the Sun\'s influence','A group of astronomers at the Center for Astrophysics, Harvard & Smithsonian and the University of Oregon has announced the first radio waves ever detected dire...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772471920.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><div><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></div><div><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>A group of astronomers at the Center for <a href=\"https://www.sciencealert.com/astronomers-detect-radio-signals-coming-directly-from-an-exoplanet-for-the-first-time\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Astrophysics</a>, Harvard &amp; Smithsonian and the University of Oregon has announced the first radio waves ever detected directly from an exoplanet. The planet, Beta Pictoris b, is a huge gas giant located about 63 light years from Earth.</div><div>The researchers used the MeerKAT radio telescope in South Africa to detect radio waves coming from the planet. Radio activity has been observed in systems with exoplanets before, but scientists were not able to rule out that the radio activity was originating in the exoplanet or from the host star. This time, the researchers could identify the emission, unit by unit, to the planet Beta Pictoris b.</div><div>What is causing the signal?</div><div>The radio waves seem to be linked with auroral activity, like the northern and southern lights on Earth.</div><div>What can a radio signal tell scientists about a planet that they can\'t visit?</div><div>Auroras are formed when particles with electrical charges interact with a planet\'s magnetic field. These interactions can also generate radio waves. The more the researchers know about the emission, the more they will be able to learn about the strength of the magnetic field of the planet.</div><div>The study indicates that the magnetic field of Beta <a href=\"https://www.sciencenews.org/article/exoplanet-aurora-radio-waves\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Pictoris</a> b is very strong, at least 1000 times stronger than Earth\'s. This planet is about 10 times bigger than Jupiter.</div><div>Eventually, the finding might help scientists understand how planets protect their own atmospheres and how they interact with the powerful wind that results from a planet\'s own star.</div><div>Yet this is not proof of an alien civilisation: even the catchy term \'radio signals from an exoplanet\' must be taken with a pinch of salt. The emission is a natural phenomenon that is linked to the magnetic environment of the planet.</div><div>Rather, it provides <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.16720v1\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">astronomers</a> with something far more useful: a new approach to the study of the invisible magnetic properties of worlds many light years distant.</div>','World Politics','[\"Legal Affairs\",\"World Politics\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772471920.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790772556282,'Sep 30, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"oshidiyapa190@gmail.com\"]',0,'Radio detected','Radio signals have been detected directly from an exoplanet.','A group of astronomers at the Center for Astrophysics, Harvard & Smithsonian and the University of Oregon has announced the first radio waves ever detected dire','[]'),('1790772758643','Why Did Typhoon Dujuan Cause So Much Damage in Japan?','1790772758643','Typhoon Dujuan had departed from Japan, but heavy rainfall, landslides and flooding had resulted in a trail of devastation in the region near Tokyo','The storm also wreaked havoc. Roads were inundated, railway services were halted and houses were in danger of being damaged. Many people were left stranded when...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772748068.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><div><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>The storm also wreaked havoc. Roads were inundated, railway services were halted and houses were in danger of being damaged. Many people were left stranded when Japan Airlines cancelled 135 flights and All Nippon Airways cancelled 140.</div><div>But how can a storm moving away cause such problems?</div><div>The greatest threat was rainfall. Dujuan dumped <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/business/environment/torrential-rains-brought-by-japan-typhoon-kill-two-nhk-says-2026-09-22/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tremendous</a> amounts of water over eastern Japan. In the island of Oshima, just south of Tokyo, over 800 millimetres of rain fell in 48 hours, twice the monthly rainfall for the island!</div><div>In this scenario, the ground can become saturated and unstable when so much rain falls in a brief time period. Landslides can occur and rivers can surge quickly, flooding surrounding towns and cities. A mudslide in the Japanese port of Yokosuka inundated a house, killing a woman in her 60s. Search and rescue teams were also combing through debris for any missing persons.</div><div>The threat from the storm was not the only one. Even as Dujuan turned east-northeast into the Pacific, the already swollen rivers and saturated ground posed threats. Heavy rains may persist until the typhoon passed, Japan\'s weather agency said.</div><div>Typhoons are a common occurrence in Japan, and each one might be hazardous in a different way due to the amount of rainfall. The image <a href=\"https://www.afp.com/en/typhoon-dujuan-leaves-four-dead-japan-45000-houses-without-power\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">demonstrates</a> that a tropical cyclone can still cause significant flooding and landslides even if it doesn\'t directly pass over the location.</div><div>For communities near rivers and steep slopes, the most perilous time of a storm can occur after a community experiences the strongest winds.</div>','Sports','[\"International News\",\"World Politics\",\"Legal Affairs\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772748068.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790864040676,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Damage','Why Did Typhoon Dujuan Cause So Much Damage in Japan?','The storm also wreaked havoc. Roads were inundated, railway services were halted and houses were in danger of being damaged. Many people were left stranded when','[]'),('1790772829524','Warner Bros vs. Coyote vs. Acme: A Box-Office Disappointment That Became a Filmmaker Victory','1790772829524','Its box office may be modest, but the film\'s journey from a Warner Bros. tax write-off to an independent theatrical release represents something far more important for smaller filmmakers: the possibility of getting their work seen','Few recent Hollywood stories illustrate the strange relationship between filmmakers and major studios better than Coyote vs. Acme. The film was completed after ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772818042.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Few recent Hollywood stories illustrate the strange relationship between filmmakers and major studios better than <em>Coyote vs. Acme</em>. The film was completed after an approximately <strong>$70 million production</strong>, tested well with audiences and featured a combination of live action and animation. Yet in 2023, Warner Bros. Discovery decided not to release it, choosing instead to take a <a href=\"https://fortune.com/2026/08/30/warner-bros-coyote-vs-acme-tax-write-off-theaters-box-office-debut/?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">tax write-off</a>. The film appeared destined to disappear without ever reaching an audience.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">That decision became controversial because the filmmakers had already done the work. Director <strong><a href=\"https://www.latimes.com/entertainment-arts/movies/story/2026-08-26/coyote-vs-acme-dave-green-will-forte-samy-burch-animation-looney-tunes-warner-bros-interview?utm_source=chatgpt.com\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Dave Green</a></strong>, screenwriter <strong>Samy Burch</strong> and their collaborators had spent years developing a movie that audiences might never see—not because it had failed at the box office, but because a corporation had decided that releasing it no longer made financial sense.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Then something unusual happened. Public pressure helped force Warner Bros. to reconsider. The studio eventually allowed the completed movie to be sold, and independent distributor <strong>Ketchup Entertainment</strong> acquired worldwide distribution rights for roughly <strong>$50 million</strong>.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">On August 28, 2026, <em>Coyote vs. Acme</em> finally reached theaters. Its opening was hardly spectacular by Hollywood standards: approximately <strong>$15.9 million in North American theaters</strong> during its first weekend. By September 6, its domestic total had reached about <strong>$34.5 million</strong>. For a $70 million production, those numbers do not represent a conventional blockbuster success. But that is precisely why the film\'s story matters.</p>','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790772818042.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790864056139,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Coyote Acme Filmmaker','Warner Bros vs. Coyote vs. Acme: A Box-Office Disappointment That Became a Filmmaker Victory','Few recent Hollywood stories illustrate the strange relationship between filmmakers and major studios better than Coyote vs. Acme. The film was completed after','[]'),('1790773521565','Instagram’s New Feature Changes What Can Appear on Your Grid','1790773521565','The new feature gives users more control over which photos and collaborations appear on their profiles without reposting someone else’s content.','Instagram is giving users a new way to shape their profile grids by allowing tagged posts from other accounts to appear alongside their own posts.The feature, r...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789474954937-1279b7236595.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<p><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/09/10/instagrams-latest-feature-lets-you-add-tagged-posts-to-your-profile-grid/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; background-color: transparent; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; white-space: pre-wrap;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Instagram</a> is giving users a new way to shape their profile grids by allowing tagged posts from other accounts to appear alongside their own posts.</p><p>The feature, rolling out this week, lets users add a post they have been tagged in directly to their main profile grid. Instagram says the update is designed to give people more control over their profiles while making it easier to showcase group photos, collaborations and other moments shared by other users.</p><p>There are several ways to add a tagged post. Users can select <a href=\"https://gulfnews.com/technology/media/instagram-now-lets-you-put-someone-elses-post-on-your-profile-grid-1.500670383\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Add to grid”</a> from the direct-message notification they receive when they are tagged, use the three-dot menu on the tagged post itself, or press and hold a post from their Tagged tab. Once added, the post appears on the user\'s main grid with a tag indicator.</p><p>The original creator keeps ownership of the post. Adding it to another person\'s grid does not create a duplicate or move the original publication, and users can remove the tagged post from their own grid whenever they want without deleting the original.</p><p>The change could be particularly useful for creator collaborations and brand campaigns. Instead of asking creators to repost the same photo or video, a tagged post can now become part of several profiles while remaining attached to the account that originally published it.</p>','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789474954937-1279b7236595.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790864127622,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Instagram Feature Appear Grid','Instagram’s New Feature Changes What Can Appear on Your Grid','Instagram is giving users a new way to shape their profile grids by allowing tagged posts from other accounts to appear alongside their own posts.The feature, r','[]'),('1790773603200','A ‘Useless Master’s’ in New York Becomes a Viral Wealth Fantasy','1790773603200','A viral post imagining life with enough family wealth to study in New York has sparked conversations about education, privilege, humanities degrees and the freedom to choose a path without immediate financial pressure.','What would you study if you never had to worry about whether your degree would lead to a high-paying job? That question is at the center of a viral post from so...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790390838575-91b7774628a5.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>What would you study if you never had to worry about whether your degree would lead to a high-paying job? That question is at the center of a viral post from social media user Carra, who wrote that if she had generational wealth, she would “definitely be doing some useless master\'s in New York.” The post quickly drew thousands of reactions online. </p><p>The joke opened the door to an oddly specific fantasy of wealthy New York life. Replies imagined living in Manhattan, attending graduate school, studying creative writing or niche humanities subjects and spending years in the city for the experience rather than for a conventional career payoff.</p><p>For many commenters, the appeal was less about the degree itself and more about the freedom surrounding it. With family wealth covering tuition, rent and everyday expenses, graduate school could become a way to meet people, explore an intellectual interest or simply experience New York without the same pressure to turn education into immediate income.</p><p>Others pushed back on the fantasy. Some argued that people with substantial generational wealth might not need another degree at all, while others pointed out that being able to pursue an expensive graduate program without worrying about employment is itself a form of privilege.</p>','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790390838575-91b7774628a5.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790938216891,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[\"oshidiishmitha@gmail.com\"]',1,'Viral','A ‘Useless Master’s’ in New York Becomes a Viral Wealth Fantasy','What would you study if you never had to worry about whether your degree would lead to a high-paying job? That question is at the center of a viral post from so','[]'),('1790773726111','$10 Million Raised, Then $10 Million More: Olivia Rodrigo\'s Festival Makes a Huge Impact','1790773726111','The singer\'s Daisy Chain Fields festival raised $10 million for organizations supporting women and girls, including reproductive health groups, before Melinda French Gates matched the amount and pushed the total to $20 million.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789127879326-f41997f5ed69.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<p>Olivia Rodrigo\'s new music festival became much more than a celebration of female artists.</p><p>It became a multimillion-dollar fundraiser for women and girls.</p><p>Rodrigo announced that her inaugural <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/olivia-rodrigo-daisy-chain-fields-aa831e6e96d6e75f315ae35633c6cd06\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Daisy Chain Fields festival</a> raised $10 million for 10 nonprofit organizations, including groups supporting reproductive health and rights, maternal health, survivors of gender-based violence and economic justice. The announcement came as advocates have raised concerns about changes to federal funding and policies affecting reproductive healthcare in the United States. </p><p>But the story did not end there.</p><p>During the festival in Irvine, California, on August 29, 2026, philanthropist <a href=\"https://abcnews.com/GMA/Culture/melinda-french-gates-matches-10m-raised-olivia-rodrigos/story?id=136074190\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Melinda French Gates</a> announced that she would match the $10 million raised, bringing the total amount generated for the nonprofit partners to $20 million. </p><p>The distinction is important: reports sometimes describe the news as Rodrigo “donating $10 million,” but the money was raised through Daisy Chain Fields and its fundraising efforts, rather than being a $10 million personal donation from Rodrigo herself. </p><p>The funds are being distributed among 10 nonprofit organizations, including Planned Parenthood, the Center for Reproductive Rights, Black Mamas Matter Alliance, Baby2Baby, FreeFrom, Jhpiego, the National Women\'s Law Center and other organizations working on issues affecting women and girls. </p><p>Rodrigo said the festival was created to demonstrate what could happen when people come together to support one another.</p>','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789127879326-f41997f5ed69.webp',NULL,'[\"10\",\"milliom\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790913486288,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1790773807880','The Installation of 2,977 Lights Recreates the Twin Towers Over New York.','1790773807880','The memorial was an aerial display of the outline of the Twin Towers, each light symbolizing a person who lost their life on September 11, 2001.','On September 9th, 2,977 lights in the shape of drones flew into the sky above New York Harbor and formed a silhouette of the Twin Towers of the World Trade Cent...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789160115589-384d714f46aa.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>On September 9th, 2,977 lights in the shape of drones flew into the sky above New York Harbor and formed a silhouette of the Twin Towers of the <a href=\"https://abc7ny.com/post/drone-show-recreates-twin-towers-honors-2977-victims-ahead-25th-anniversary-911-attacks-new-york/19814308/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">World Trade</a> Center. The presentation came two days earlier than the 25th anniversary of 9/11.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>The overall name for the installation was “2,977 Lights Over New York Harbor,” with one light for each person who died in the attacks on the World Trade Center, Pentagon and the flight 93. Eventually, the drones built the towers, as per their original architectural scale, in the same way that the image had vanished from the New York skyline 25 years ago.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>The project was created with the input of relatives of the victims of 9/11, survivors and first responders. Their participation was planned to enhance the exhibition of the memorial rather than just a large-scale technical performance, so that it would be more personal and closer to the victims of the attacks and their<a href=\"https://skyelementsdrones.com/september11\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> aftermath.</a></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>The <a href=\"https://www.designboom.com/art/lights-twin-towers-new-york-harbor-25-years-after-9-11/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">illuminated</a> towers joined New York\'s annual memorial, the Tribute in Light, which is a memorial where powerful beams are shone into the night sky in the area where the World Trade Center used to be. The combination of the two displays was a way to provide a different visual reminder of buildings and the people who lived or worked there.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span>The towers are still very open to those who lived that day, 9/11. The buildings are mainly known to younger generations through photographs, recordings and stories. The installation of the drone was an opportunity to visually present this lost facet of the city\'s skyline and to stay focused on the lives behind the number 2,977.</span></p>','Business','[]','Home - Editors Picks','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789160115589-384d714f46aa.webp',NULL,'[\"the\",\"installation\",\"of\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790864616813,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Lights Twin Towers York','The Installation of 2,977 Lights Recreates the Twin Towers Over New York.','On September 9th, 2,977 lights in the shape of drones flew into the sky above New York Harbor and formed a silhouette of the Twin Towers of the World Trade Cent','[]'),('1790773866607','Lou\'s Lighthouse is a new Initiative that provides safe and stable housing and support for women recovering from addiction.','1790773866607','The new charity, Lou\'s Lighthouse, was founded in Oxford to help women overcome addiction, particularly by offering something that can be challenging during recovery: A safe and stable home. The charity\'s goal is to provide a place that women can stay and get help to rebuild their lives','The organisation was founded with the premise that recovery isn\'t only about not using substances anymore. Having a stable living environment, healthy relations...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789334942987-5c1adb7a2133.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;The organisation was founded with the premise that recovery isn\'t only about not using <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c70l7jnzgg1o\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; font-size: 17px; text-align: justify;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">substances</a> anymore. Having a stable living environment, healthy relationships and practical support can also make a significant difference to keeping someone in recovery. It is hoped that Lou\'s Lighthouse will be a safer place for women who may be at risk of homelessness or unstable housing.','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789334942987-5c1adb7a2133.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1790907425145,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'stable','Lou\'s Lighthouse is a new Initiative that provides safe and stable housing and support for women recovering from addiction.','The organisation was founded with the premise that recovery isn\'t only about not using substances anymore. Having a stable living environment, healthy relations','[]'),('1790773926102','Forty Love Gives Fans a First Look at Romeo Beckham’s Acting Debut','1790773926102','Paul Kircher and Romeo Beckham take on rival tennis players in the upcoming French film arriving in theaters this November.','New promotional images from the French tennis drama Forty Love are giving viewers their first closer look at Paul Kircher and Romeo Beckham as two rivals prepar...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789474582794-42f0cf7b2633.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>New promotional images from the French tennis drama <a href=\"https://www.cosmopolitan.com/entertainment/movies/a73689118/romeo-beckham-forty-love/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Forty Love</a> are giving viewers their first closer look at Paul Kircher and Romeo Beckham as two rivals preparing for a major tournament in Paris.</p><p>Kircher plays Sacha Gallo, a young and ambitious tennis player whose focus is winning a Paris title. His preparations are disrupted when he encounters a charismatic rival played by Romeo Beckham, who makes his acting debut in the film. </p><p>The newly released images show the two actors in contrasting tennis looks. Beckham appears with a shaved head, tattoos and a headband, while Kircher is shown with curly hair as the pair appear beneath large “ROMA” banners.</p><p>The visual differences have quickly caught the attention of tennis fans, with some comparing the characters\' appearances to real-world stars including Carlos Alcaraz and Rafael Nadal. The similarities appear to be fan observations based on the players\' styling and on-court image rather than confirmed inspiration for the characters.</p><p>Directed by Pierre-Ange Carlotti, Forty Love combines the pressure of professional tennis with a <a href=\"https://www.outsports.com/2026/9/11/24143159/forty-love-gay-tennis-movie-romeo-beckham-alcaraz-nadal/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">relationship</a> that develops between its central characters. The story follows Sacha as his pursuit of success becomes complicated by his connection with his rival.</p>','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789474582794-42f0cf7b2633.webp',NULL,'[\"forty\",\"love\",\"gives\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790865834730,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Forty Love Look Romeo','Forty Love Gives Fans a First Look at Romeo Beckham’s Acting Debut','New promotional images from the French tennis drama Forty Love are giving viewers their first closer look at Paul Kircher and Romeo Beckham as two rivals prepar','[]'),('1790863608681','Istanbul\'s airport has surpassed London Heathrow as the busiest and most connected airport in the world.','1790863608681','For years, London Heathrow has been one of the world’s most important gateways for international travellers. These days, it\'s another European airport in the number one spot.','No airport is more synonymous with international travel than London Heathrow. Heathrow airport is the busiest international airport in the UK on the west side o...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789959509051-29ad03f54ce0.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;No airport is more synonymous with international travel than London Heathrow. Heathrow airport is the busiest international airport in the UK on the west side of London with over 80 million passengers passing through every year. It links Britain to hundreds of other destinations around the world, and it\'s been among the busiest airports in the world.','Sports','[\"News\",\"International News\",\"Criminal Cases\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1789959509051-29ad03f54ce0.webp',NULL,'[\"istanbul\",\"airport\",\"surpassed\",\"london\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790863967944,'Oct 1, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'London Heathrow','Istanbul\'s airport has surpassed London Heathrow as the busiest and most connected airport in the world.','No airport is more synonymous with international travel than London Heathrow. Heathrow airport is the busiest international airport in the UK on the west side o','[]'),('1790863684028','New Camino Trail Offers Visitors a Quieter Side of Dubrovnik Beyond the Crowds','1790863684028','Long celebrated for its medieval architecture and Adriatic coastline, Dubrovnik has also become one of Europe\'s busiest tourist destinations.','A newly established long-distance hiking route, however, is encouraging visitors to explore the region beyond the city\'s famous walls while promoting a more sus...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790863658673.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>A newly established long-distance hiking route, however, is encouraging visitors to explore the region beyond the city\'s famous walls while promoting a more sustainable approach to tourism.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The <strong>Camino Dubrovnik–Međugorje</strong>, <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/travel/article/20260717-a-new-way-to-see-the-worlds-most-overcrowded-city\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">officially opened earlier</a> this year, stretches approximately <strong>145 kilometers</strong> from Dubrovnik to the pilgrimage town of Međugorje in Bosnia and Herzegovina. Inspired by Europe\'s historic Camino pilgrimage routes, the trail combines cultural heritage, natural landscapes, and centuries-old travel paths that once connected coastal trade centers with inland communities.</p><h2><b>A Different Perspective on Dubrovnik</b></h2><div><b><br></b></div><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The route begins at the <strong>Church of St. James</strong> in Dubrovnik and winds through villages, forests, mountain trails, and historic settlements before crossing the international border into Bosnia and Herzegovina.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Along the journey, hikers pass landmarks including medieval water systems, former trade routes, religious pilgrimage paths, and panoramic viewpoints overlooking the Adriatic Sea.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Tourism officials say the initiative aims to introduce travelers to parts of the Dubrovnik region that many visitors never experience while reducing pressure on the city\'s heavily visited historic center.</p>','Sports','[\"Criminal Cases\",\"Politics\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790863658673.webp',NULL,'[\"new\",\"camino\",\"trail\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790907418244,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Visitors Beyond','New Camino Trail Offers Visitors a Quieter Side of Dubrovnik Beyond the Crowds','A newly established long-distance hiking route, however, is encouraging visitors to explore the region beyond the city\'s famous walls while promoting a more sus','[]'),('1790863774441','Two Killed After Firefighting Helicopters Collide in Greece; British Pilot Survives','1790863774441','Two crew members were killed after two firefighting helicopters collided mid-air while battling a major wildfire west of Athens on Sunday','Marking a tragic setback as Greece continues to confront one of its most challenging wildfire seasons.The victims were identified as a Danish pilot and a Greek ...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790863741895.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span></p><figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790863743982.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Marking a tragic setback as Greece continues to confront one of its most challenging wildfire seasons.</p><p data-start=\"352\" data-end=\"664\">The victims were identified as a Danish pilot and a Greek fire service liaison officer. A British pilot and a Greek fire service coordinator aboard the second helicopter <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c1417713ve6o\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">survived the collision</a>, suffering only minor injuries. Both were taken to hospital for observation and are reported to be in stable condition.</p><p data-start=\"666\" data-end=\"1087\">The accident occurred approximately 65 kilometers west of Athens near the Attica–Boeotia border, where firefighters have been battling a rapidly spreading wildfire. Video footage circulating online shows one Bell helicopter striking the rotor blades of another before one aircraft burst into flames and crashed into a nearby ravine. The second helicopter</p>','Sports','[\"Elections\",\"Law\",\"Golf\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790863741895.webp',NULL,'[\"two\",\"killed\",\"after\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790907403035,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Greece Pilot','Two Killed After Firefighting Helicopters Collide in Greece; British Pilot Survives','Marking a tragic setback as Greece continues to confront one of its most challenging wildfire seasons.The victims were identified as a Danish pilot and a Greek','[]'),('1790863849443','Why Do Hot Springs Really Get Hot? The Solution Begins Far Below Your Feet','1790863849443','There is absolutely no heat at the beginning of the bubbling water. On a long, deep detour, it is rainfall.','With no stove or fire in sight, the water rising directly out of the ground and already steaming appears almost miraculous. The true explanation begins far earl...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/content/1788654824141-295b42c5a2bf.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>With no stove or fire in sight, the water rising directly out of the ground and already <a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/media/images/hot-springs-alaska-caused-geothermal-activity-underground\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-family: &quot;Times New Roman&quot;; font-size: 12pt;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">steaming</a> appears almost miraculous. The true explanation begins far earlier than most people realize and much below the surface. Before it ever reappears as something you would like to swim in, the majority of hot springs start out as perfectly normal rain or groundwater that seeps through fissures and faults in the Earth\'s crust, often for years.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">What, then, heats it during the process? Depending on the location, there are two primary routes. Groundwater can come into direct touch with shallow pockets of magma, or molten rock that is relatively close to the surface, in areas where volcanism is active. This causes the water to heat up significantly as it goes by. In locations without volcanic activity, heat is generated by something slower and more consistent: the <a href=\"https://www.usgs.gov/news/featured-story/its-a-hot-topic-geothermal-energy-and-how-usgs-science-could-help-harness-it\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">geothermal </a>gradient, which is simply the fact that rock temperature rises as you go deeper beneath. When water seeps far enough, it finally comes into contact with rock that is hot enough to warm it without the need for magma.</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">The water does not stay down there either way. When heated, it loses density relative to the surrounding cooler water, which causes it to rise through fissures and cracks until it eventually emerges as a hot spring. A hot spring can become a geyser by periodically</p>','World Politics','[\"World Politics\",\"Legal Affairs\",\"Law\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/content/1788654824141-295b42c5a2bf.webp',NULL,'[\"why\",\"do\",\"hot\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790907275338,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Begins Far','Why Do Hot Springs Really Get Hot? The Solution Begins Far Below Your Feet','With no stove or fire in sight, the water rising directly out of the ground and already steaming appears almost miraculous. The true explanation begins far earl','[]'),('1790865765556','Two Killed After Firefighting Helicopters Collide in Greece; British Pilot Survives','1790865765556','Two crew members were killed after two firefighting helicopters collided mid-air while battling a major wildfire west of Athens on Sunday','Two crew members were killed after two firefighting helicopters collided mid-air while battling a major wildfire west of Athens on Sunday','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790865756249.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;','Sports','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1790865756249.webp',NULL,'[\"two\",\"killed\",\"qw\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790907180637,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Two Killed Firefighting Helicopters','Two Killed After Firefighting Helicopters Collide in Greece; British Pilot Survives','Two crew members were killed after two firefighting helicopters collided mid-air while battling a major wildfire west of Athens on Sunday','[]'),('1790901628203','Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland Unite Around Self Determination','1790901628203','The leaders of the Scottish National Party, Plaid Cymru and Sinn Féin signed a joint agreement calling for self-determination and closer ties with the European Union.','Leaders from Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland have joined forces in a new push for constitutional change, declaring that their nations have the right to det...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790249212630-68ed9fbc0a2f.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Leaders from <a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/14/leaders-of-scotland-wales-northern-ireland-unite-for-self-determination\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland</a> have joined forces in a new push for constitutional change, declaring that their nations have the right to determine their own futures and saying they see those futures within the <a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c62enegxyl9o\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">European Union.</a></p><p>The agreement was signed in Cardiff on Sept. 14 by John Swinney of Scotland’s Scottish National Party, Rhun ap Iorwerth of Wales’ Plaid Cymru and Michelle O’Neill of Northern Ireland’s Sinn Féin, alongside Sinn Féin president Mary Lou McDonald. The leaders met in their political-party roles rather than as representatives of their governments.</p><p>The memorandum states that “our nations have the right to self-determination” and argues that no Westminster government should prevent people in Scotland, Wales or Northern Ireland from deciding their political future. It also declares, “The future of our nations belongs in the European Union.”</p><p>The three parties have different constitutional goals. The SNP supports Scottish independence, Plaid Cymru supports Welsh independence, while Sinn Féin campaigns for Northern Ireland to leave the United Kingdom and join a united Ireland. Their positions also differ over when and how votes on constitutional change should take place.</p><p>Scotland has already held an independence referendum. In 2014, voters rejected independence by 55.3% to 44.7%, with Scotland remaining part of the United Kingdom. Swinney has called for another referendum, while the UK government has opposed an immediate new vote.</p>','Sports','[\"News\",\"International News\",\"Criminal Cases\",\"Politics\",\"Congress\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790249212630-68ed9fbc0a2f.webp',NULL,'[\"scotland\",\"wales\",\"plais\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1790901731891,'Oct 2, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,'Scotland Wales Northern Ireland','Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland Unite Around Self Determination','Leaders from Scotland, Wales and Northern Ireland have joined forces in a new push for constitutional change, declaring that their nations have the right to det','[]'),('1791028945238','Christa Pike’s Death Sentence Takes an Unexpected Turn in Tennessee','1791028945238','Pike was scheduled to become the first woman executed by Tennessee in more than 200 years, but the state stopped the procedure after she remained alive following two doses of lethal-injection drugs.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790853410231-42b8fbe72c9c.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4 Fallback&quot;, serif; font-size: 18px;\">&nbsp;</span>Christa Pike’s scheduled execution in Tennessee took an unexpected turn Wednesday night after the state’s attempt to carry out her lethal injection was halted and she was taken to a medical facility.&nbsp;</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Pike, 50, had been scheduled to become the <strong><a href=\"https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cq8r6rjdvlx6o\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">first woman executed by Tennessee in more than 200 years</a></strong>. She was convicted of the 1995 killing of 19-year-old <a href=\"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/1/us-supreme-court-clears-way-for-christa-pikes-execution-in-tennessee\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Colleen Slemmer</a> when Pike was 18.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">The execution itself had already been delayed earlier Wednesday. The U.S. Court of Appeals for the Sixth Circuit issued a temporary stay about an hour before the scheduled execution while considering whether claims about Pike’s childhood sexual abuse had received proper consideration. The U.S. Supreme Court later overturned that stay, allowing Tennessee to proceed.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">After the Supreme Court ruling, prison officials resumed preparations at Riverbend Maximum Security Institution in Nashville. Pike was administered two doses of the drug used in Tennessee’s lethal-injection protocol, according to court filings from her attorneys.</p><p class=\"isSelectedEnd\">Media witnesses reported that Pike remained alive after the second dose. Her attorneys subsequently filed an emergency motion seeking to halt the execution, while the Tennessee Department of Correction confirmed that Pike had been transported to an off-site medical facility. Officials did not initially provide details about her condition.</p>','International News','[\"News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1790853410231-42b8fbe72c9c.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1791029050935,'Oct 3, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:03','2026-10-20 07:59:59','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1791551695562','Down Syndrome: What Does It Look like When a Different Kind of Joy Comes to a Home?','1791551695562','But beyond the diagnosis, there is a person with his/her personality, habits, frustrations, laughter, and position in the family.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791551668156.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>The arrival of a kid with down syndrome changes a home. Not because it is difficult for them, or because they are no longer able to enjoy a <a href=\"https://www.cdc.gov/birth-defects/about/down-syndrome.html.com\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; font-size: 17px; text-align: justify;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">fulfilling</a> life. It usually happens as the result of noticing things that the family may not have been conscious of before, such as how the person communicates, how long it takes him to learn something, what comforts him and how differently each family member experiences the world. Down syndrome is the result of an individual being born with an extra copy of the 21st chromosome, some of whose genes can <a href=\"https://ndss.org/myths-truths\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline; font-family: Lora, Georgia, serif; font-size: 17px; text-align: justify;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">influence</a> physical and intellectual development.&nbsp;','Business','[\"Legal Affairs\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon',NULL,'Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791551668156.webp',NULL,'[\"zxc\",\"Elon Musk\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1791940997952,'Oct 14, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:01','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[\"qwert@gmail.com\"]',0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1791552310492','Search Underway After Medical Jet Disappears Off Nantucket','1791552310492','Air traffic controllers lost contact with a medical transfer plane with six people on board early Saturday as it flew from Bermuda to Boston.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791552298859.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;<div>According to Skyport, the airport operator, the plane left L.F. Wade International Airport in Bermuda around 12:41 a.m. on Oct. 3. It had six on board, four crew and two passengers, and was scheduled for a flight to Boston Logan International Airport. (Skyport Bermuda)&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>So, where are rescuers looking?&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The focus of the search is the waters south of Nantucket, an island off the <a href=\"https://apnews.com/article/plane-search-bermuda-boston-nantucket-ccb6014ac35e2af11879e28e6c8527df\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Massachusetts</a> coast. The Coast Guard has sent aircraft and boats to the area, including an HC 144 aircraft, an MH 60 helicopter, a 47-foot motor lifeboat and the cutter William Sparling. According to local reports, the search area was about 13 nautical miles south of Nantucket.&nbsp;</div><div><br></div><div>The missing aircraft is identified as tail number C GRJP and is operated by Latitude Air Ambulance, an Ontario based company that provides medical air transportation. The company\'s flight operations director told NBC News the situation was <a href=\"https://www.royalgazette.com/general/news/article/20261003/search-launched-for-missing-air-ambulance/\" style=\"border-width: 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: currentcolor; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(234, 88, 12); text-decoration: underline;\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">troubling</a>, but added that it was not enough to determine what happened to the aircraft.</div><div><br></div><div>The cause of the loss of communication, the location of the aircraft and the condition of the six people on board have yet to be confirmed. The National Transportation Safety Board was able to report at the time of its initial statement that it was collecting data about the incident.&nbsp;</div>','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon',NULL,'Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791552298859.webp',NULL,'[\"Mark Zuckerberg\"]','[]','5 min read',6,1791941054794,'Oct 14, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:01','2026-10-20 08:28:56','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1791755401513','A New Wild Cat Species Has Been Identified After More Than 100 Years','1791755401513','Named Leopardus tilcayo, the small spotted feline was found to be genetically distinct from other tiger cats after researchers examined its DNA.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791755374464.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p>The research also changed scientists’ understanding of South America’s tiger cats. What was previously considered one species is now understood to include five distinct species, showing how genetic analysis can reveal differences that are difficult to identify from appearance alone. </p><p>And scientists believe the tilcayo may not be the last surprise. Small wild cats are difficult to study because they are elusive and often live in remote forests, meaning other distinct species could still be waiting to be identified.</p><p>For now, researchers know relatively little about the tilcayo’s behavior, diet and reproduction. Its known Yungas habitat also faces threats from deforestation, agriculture, fires and mining, making further research important for understanding how the species can be protected. </p><br class=\"Apple-interchange-newline\">','Business','[\"Interviews\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1791755374464.webp',NULL,'[\"Nico Santoro\"]','[]','5 min read',1,1791940923042,'Oct 14, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:01','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1792063094027','NYC Reaches Deal to Phase Out Horse Carriages by 2028','1792063094027','Mayor Zohran Mamdani and City Council Speaker Julie Menin have backed a proposed phase-out by June 2028, with a vote scheduled for October 22 and new provisions for workers and retired horses.',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1791990931781-5177ca99dc76.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p>&nbsp;Mamdani said his administration would work to protect both workers and horses as&nbsp;<a href=\"https://wsj.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#888888] font-medium no-underline hover:text-[#555555]\" style=\"color: rgb(136, 136, 136); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom-width: medium; border-bottom-style: none; border-bottom-color: currentcolor; box-shadow: none;\">the</a> city prepares for the proposed change. Menin has argued that the busy park environment raises safety concerns for <a href=\"https://wsj.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" class=\"text-[#888888] font-medium no-underline hover:text-[#555555]\" style=\"color: rgb(136, 136, 136); font-weight: 500; text-decoration: none; border-bottom-width: medium; border-bottom-style: none; border-bottom-color: currentcolor; box-shadow: none;\">horses</a>, passengers, pedestrians and carriage drivers.</p><p>The revised proposal includes a workforce transition program that the city must develop by April 2027. The plan would connect carriage drivers and other affected workers with new employment opportunities, including career counseling, job referrals and career fairs, with possible options in public transportation, hospitality and tourism.</p><p>The legislation also addresses what will happen to the horses after carriage operations end. The city would establish a program to help arrange their humane retirement, including provisions intended to prevent them from being sold for slaughter or transferred to other horse-drawn carriage businesses.</p>','Entrepreneurship','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya',NULL,'Published','https://washingtontimes.s3.us-east-005.backblazeb2.com/articles/1791990931781-5177ca99dc76.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',2,1792063525845,'Oct 15, 2026','2026-10-15 05:48:14','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1792410585355','Trump’s Overtures to Putin Put Republican Candidates in Hot Seat','1792410585355','GOP politicians in a number of tight races are breaking with Trump on Russia policy ahead of midterms','President Trump’s surprise diesel deal with Russia and decision to waive sanctions on Moscow have become a headache for Republican candidates with just two week...','<p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">&nbsp;President Trump’s surprise diesel deal with <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/russia\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Russia</a> and decision to waive sanctions on Moscow have become a headache for Republican candidates with just two weeks to go before the midterms.&nbsp;</p><figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792410272019_1792410272165.jpg\" alt=\"qwert\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px; display: block;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%; box-sizing: border-box;\"><span class=\"image-caption\" style=\"font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; color: #64748b; margin-right: 12px;\">qwert</span><span class=\"image-credit\" style=\"font-size: 10px; font-weight: bold; font-family: monospace, sans-serif; color: #64748b; text-transform: uppercase; margin-left: auto; text-align: right;\">(PHOTO: ABCD)</span></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">In interviews and town halls, Republicans are being pressed on why now is the time to go soft on Vladimir Putin. Some of them are breaking with Trump rather than defend his string of Russia-friendly decisions.</p>','News','[\"U.S. News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792410272019_1792410272165.jpg',NULL,'[\"Bernard Arnault & family\"]','[]','5 min read',1,1792410772689,'Oct 19, 2026','2026-10-19 11:49:45','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'Trump Republican Candidates','Trump’s Overtures to Putin Put Republican Candidates in Hot Seat','President Trump’s surprise diesel deal with Russia and decision to waive sanctions on Moscow have become a headache for Republican candidates with just two week','[]'),('1792414107187','sdfg','1792414107187','dfg','ghf','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792414094417.webp\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure>&nbsp;ghf','News','[\"U.S. News\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','Imaya','writer@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792414094417.webp',NULL,'[\"erty\",\"fghjkl\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1792414242040,'Oct 19, 2026','2026-10-19 12:48:27','2026-10-20 07:59:58','[]',1,'sdfg','sdfg','ghf','[]'),('1792479524994','U.S. Stocks Mostly Higher as AI Credit Worries Abate','1792479524994','Traders pared back bets that tech firms chasing the AI boom had overextended themselves and shifted focus to coming AI earnings',NULL,'<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792479517895_1792479518004.jpg\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">&nbsp;The Dow Jones Industrial Average edged down 36.38 points, or 0.07%, to 51966.03. While the S&amp;P 500 gained 31.29 points, or 0.41%, to 7690.73 and the tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite jumped 290.85 points, or 1.11%, to 26430.89, regaining some of the losses from its worst week since June.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">Treasury yields rose as bond investors braced for a potential rate hike from the <a data-type=\"subject\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/subject/federal-reserve\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Federal Reserve</a> in response to the latest bout of energy-driven inflation.</p>','Business','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','liya','oshidiishmitha@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792479517895_1792479518004.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',6,1792489557525,'Oct 20, 2026','2026-10-20 06:58:45','2026-10-20 18:12:47','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('1792483310149','U.S. Stocks Rise as Iran Escalation Fears Subside','1792483310149','President Trump said the U.S. would not strike Iran before the mid-term elections',NULL,'<div data-type=\"image\" data-inset_type=\"\" data-sub_type=\"\" class=\"media-layout css-13plya0-Layout-baseCss ertdlv30\" data-layout=\"inline\"><figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792483267922_1792483268495.jpg\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><figcaption class=\"eihhvrm0 css-1n6fay2-FigcaptionItem e1ofw1fq21\" style=\"direction: ltr;\"><span class=\"e1m33gv80 css-426zcb-CaptionSpan e1m33gv81\"><span style=\"font-family: Exchange, Georgia, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, &quot;Source Serif 4&quot;, serif, serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;</span>All three major U.S. stock indexes ended higher on Friday.</span> <span class=\"css-7jz429-Credit eq0esvu0\">Jeenah Moon/Reuters</span></figcaption></div><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">U.S. stocks rose after President <a data-type=\"person\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/person/donald-trump\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Donald Trump</a> said the U.S. would not strike <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/iran\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Iran</a> before the mid-term elections, quelling concerns about an escalation of the Middle East war and related energy-market chaos.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">The Dow Jones Industrial Average gained 423.31 points, or 0.83%, to 51654.95. The S&amp;P 500 rose 46.18 points, or 0.59%, to 7811.54, closing near all-time highs. The tech-heavy Nasdaq Composite climbed 172.83 points, or 0.64%, to 27366.17.</p>','World Politics','[\"Upcoming Brands\",\"Books\"]','None (Category and Search Only)','sophia','oshidiyapa190@gmail.com','Published','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792483267922_1792483268495.jpg',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',13,1792483611542,'Oct 20, 2026','2026-10-20 08:01:50','2026-10-20 18:13:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[{\"id\":18,\"name\":\"rayon\",\"email\":\"oshidiishmitha@gmail.com\",\"slug\":\"rayon\"},{\"id\":5,\"name\":\"Imaya\",\"email\":\"writer@gmail.com\",\"slug\":\"imaya\"}]'),('1792502569875','The Northeast Climate Revolt','1792502569875','Anti-fossil fuel policies that raise utility bills have Democrats in the region playing defense this election year.','Voters are revolting against high energy prices across the country, and Republicans are taking most of the blame as the party in power in Washington. But an und...','<figure style=\"float: left; margin: 8px 24px 16px 0px; width: 450px; clear: left; max-width: 100%;\"><img src=\"https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792502554018_1792502554355.jpg\" alt=\"Article image\" style=\"width: 100%; border-radius: 12px;\"><div style=\"display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-top: 6px; font-family: sans-serif; width: 100%;\"></div></figure><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">&nbsp;Voters are revolting against high energy prices across the country, and Republicans are taking most of the blame as the party in power in Washington. But an under-reported story is that Democrats are on defense in the Northeast, where utility bills have spiked because of green energy mandates and progressive hostility to fossil fuels. It’s about time.</p><p data-type=\"paragraph\" class=\"css-1qg6i2u eiyqc160\">Electricity and heating bills have shot up more in the Northeast than elsewhere. Over the last six years, residential electric rates have climbed by about 20% to 30% in most states, yet far more in Maine (92%), New York (59%), <a data-type=\"place\" href=\"https://www.wsj.com/topics/place/rhode-island\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ekxajjj0 css-i0lbhy-OverridedLink\" style=\"display: inline; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); text-decoration: none; transition-property: color, fill; transition-duration: 200ms, 200ms; transition-timing-function: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1), cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.5, 1); border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(34, 34, 34);\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rhode Island</a> (45%) and Massachusetts (43%). Some households are paying hundreds of dollars more a month than they did a few years ago.</p>','Business','[\"World Politics\",\"Elections\"]',NULL,'liya','oshidiishmitha@gmail.com','Rejected','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/article_img_1792502554018_1792502554355.jpg',NULL,'[\"Alex Morgan\"]','[]','5 min read',0,1792502570192,'Oct 20, 2026','2026-10-20 13:22:50','2026-10-20 18:12:47','[]',1,'Revolt',NULL,'Voters are revolting against high energy prices across the country, and Republicans are taking most of the blame as the party in power in Washington. But an und','[]'),('pending_1788583594138','Writer1 Breakthrough Tech Innovation Review Article','pending_1788583594138','Tech review content...','Tech review content...','<p>Pending review body for writer1@gmail.com</p>','Tech','[]','None (Category and Search Only)','Mayon','writer1@gmail.com','Trash','https://f005.backblazeb2.com/file/timeschicago/articles/thumb_pending_1788583594138_1790641374994_1790641375204.webp',NULL,'[]','[]','5 min read',0,1788586413887,'Sep 5, 2026','2026-10-11 16:20:06','2026-10-20 08:00:01','[]',1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'[]'),('post_live_test_1788578232555','Backblaze B2 Upload Live Verification Article','b2-upload-live-verification',NULL,NULL,'<p>Hello world!</p><img src=\"/api/webp-proxy?url=https%3A%2F%2Ff005.backblazeb2.com%2Ffile%2Ftimeschicago%2Farticles%2Farticle_post_live_test_1788578232555_img_1788578235080_0.png\" alt=\"Test inline\">','Business','[]',NULL,'Imaya','wr